lass divides up into teams to work on mixed-signal integrated circuit designs. The chips are fabricated to be tested the following term. Lectures cover use of computer-aided design tools, design issues specific to the projects, and chip integration issues. This course shares lectures with E4350, but the complexity requirements of integrated circuits are higher...", "similarity_score": 1.200635552406311}, {"course_title": "DIGITAL SYSTEMS LABORATORY", "course_code": "ELEN E3082", "department": "Electrical Engineering", "department_code": "ELEN", "points": "1", "instructor": "Kenneth Shepard", "scheduled_time_start": 250, "scheduled_time_end": 400, "scheduled_days": "M", "type": "LABORATORY", "content": "DIGITAL SYSTEMS LABORATORY (ELEN E3082)\\n        Course Subtitle: DIGITAL SYSTEMS LABORATOR\\n        Description: Companion lab course for CSEE W3827. Experiments cover such topics as logic gates; flip-flops; shift registers; counters; combinational logic circuits; sequential logic circuits; programmable logic devices. The lab generally meets on alternate weeks.\\n        Prerequisites: CSEE W3827\\n    ", "similarity_score": 1.3382201194763184}, {"course_title": "COMMUNICATION CIRCUITS", "course_code": "ELEN E4314", "department": "Electrical Engineering", "department_code": "ELEN", "points": "3", "instructor": "Emily Naviasky", "scheduled_time_start": 250, "scheduled_time_end": 400, "scheduled_days": "R", "type": "LECTURE", "content": "COMMUNICATION CIRCUITS (ELEN E4314)\\n        Course Subtitle: \\n        Description: Principles of electronic circuits used in the generation, transmission, and reception of signal waveforms, as used in analog and digital communication systems. Nonlinearity and distortion; power amplifiers; tuned amplifiers; oscillators; multipliers and mixers; modulators and demodulators; phase-locked loops. An extensive design project is an integral part of the course.\\n        Prerequisites: \\n    ", "similarity_score": 1.3475964069366455}, {"