{'event': 'on_chain_stream', 'run_id': '019b9093-c32e-71a2-8605-55779bfab76c', 'name': 'LangGraph', 'tags': [], 'metadata': {'thread_id': '2de77b04-7c32-47ec-84dc-81f3861507d4'}, 'data': {'chunk': {'tools': {'messages': [ToolMessage(content='{"courses": [{"course_title": "Analog-Digital Interfaces in VLSI", "course_code": "ELEN E6316", "department": "Electrical Engineering", "department_code": "ELEN", "points": "3", "instructor": "Timothy Dickson", "scheduled_time_start": 420, "scheduled_time_end": 570, "scheduled_days": "T", "type": "LECTURE", "content": "Analog-Digital Interfaces in VLSI (ELEN E6316)\\n        Course Subtitle: Analog-Digital Interfaces\\n        Description: Analog-to-digital and digital-to-analog conversion techniques for very large scale integrated circuits and systems. Precision sampling; quantization; A/D and D/A converter architectures and metrics; Nyquist architectures; oversampling architectures; correction techniques; system considerations. A design project is an integral part of this course.\\n        Prerequisites: \\n    ", "similarity_score": 1.1390514373779297}, {"course_title": "VLSI DESIGN LABORATORY", "course_code": "ELEN E6350", "department": "Electrical Engineering", "department_code": "ELEN", "points": "3", "instructor": "Mingoo Seok", "scheduled_time_start": 880, "scheduled_time_end": 955, "scheduled_days": "TR", "type": "LABORATORY", "content": "VLSI DESIGN LABORATORY (ELEN E6350)\\n        Course Subtitle: \\n        Description: Design of a CMOS mixed-signal integrated circuit. The class divides up into teams to work on mixed-signal integrated circuit designs. The chips are fabricated to be tested the following term. Lectures cover use of computer-aided design tools, design issues specific to the projects, and chip integration issues. This course shares lectures with E4350, but the complexity requirements of integrated circuits are higher...", "similarity_score": 1.2171201705932617}, {"course_title": "PHOTONIC INTEGRATED CIRCUITS", "course_code": "ELEN E6414", "department": "Electrical Engineering", "department_code": "ELEN", "points": "3", "instructor": "Michal Lipson", "scheduled_time_start": 970, "scheduled_time_end": 1120, "scheduled_days": "W", "type": "LECTURE", "content": "PHOTONIC INTEGRATED CIRCUITS (ELEN E6414)\\n        Course Subtitle: PHOTONIC INTEGRATED CIRCU\\n        Description: Photonic integrated circuits are important subsystem components for telecommunications, optically controlled radar, optical signal processing, and photonic local area networks. An introduction to the devices and the design of these circuits. Principle and modeling of dielectric waveguides (including silica on silicon and InP based materials), waveguide devices (simple and star couple...", "similarity_score": 1.2714366912841797}, {"course_title": "DIGITAL SYSTEMS LABORATORY", "course_code": "ELEN E3082", "department": "Electrical Engineering", "department_code": "ELEN", "points": "1", "instructor": "Kenneth Shepard", "scheduled_time_start": 250, "scheduled_time_end": 400, "scheduled_days": "M", "type": "LABORATORY", "content": "DIGITAL SYSTEMS LABORATORY (ELEN E3082)\\n        Course Subtitle: DIGITAL SYSTEMS LABORATOR\\n        Description: Companion lab course for CSEE W3827. Experiments cover such topics as logic gates; flip-flops; shift registers; counters; combinational logic circuits; sequential logic circuits; programmable logic devices. The lab generally meets on alternate weeks.\\n        Prerequisites: CSEE W3827\\n    ", "similarity_score": 1.3084306716918945}, {"course_title": "COMMUNICATION CIRCUITS", "course_code": "ELEN E4314", "department": "Electrical Engineering", "department_code": "ELEN", "points": "3", "instructor": "Emily Naviasky", "scheduled_time_start": 250, "scheduled_time_end": 400, "scheduled_days": "R", "type": "LECTURE", "content": "COMMUNICATION CIRCUITS (ELEN E4314)\\n        Course Subtitle: \\n        Description: Principles of electronic circuits used in the generation, transmission, and reception of signal waveforms, as used in analog and digital communication systems. Nonlinearity and distortion; power amplifiers; tuned amplifiers; oscillators; multipliers and mixers; modulators and demodulators; phase-locked loops. An extensive design project is an integral part of the course.\\n        Prerequisites: \\n    ", "similarity_score": 1.3107632398605347}, {"course_title": "ADV ANALOG INTEGRATED CIRCUITS", "course_code": "ELEN E6312", "department": "Electrical Engineering", "department_code": "ELEN", "points": "3", "instructor": "Harish Krishnaswamy", "scheduled_time_start": 250, "scheduled_time_end": 400, "scheduled_days": "T", "type": "LECTURE", "content": "ADV ANALOG INTEGRATED CIRCUITS (ELEN E6312)\\n        Course Subtitle: ADV ANALOG INTEGRATED CIR\\n        Description: Integrated circuit device characteristics and models; temperature- and supply-independent biasing; IC operational amplifier analysis and design and their applications; feedback amplifiers, stability and frequency compensation techniques; noise in circuits and low-noise design; mismatch in circuits and low-offset design. Computer-aided analysis techniques are used in homework(s) or ...", "similarity_score": 1.3218504190444946}, {"course_title": "DIGITAL COMMUNICATIONS", "course_code": "ELEN E4702", "department": "Electrical Engineering", "department_code": "ELEN", "points": "3", "instructor": "Alexei Ashikhmin", "scheduled_time_start": 420, "scheduled_time_end": 570, "scheduled_days": "W", "type": "LECTURE", "content": "DIGITAL COMMUNICATIONS (ELEN E4702)\\n        Course Subtitle: \\n        Description: Digital communications for both point-to-point and switched applications is further developed. Optimum receiver structures and transmitter signal shaping for both binary and M-ary signal transmission. An introduction to block codes and convolutional codes, with application to space communications.\\n        Prerequisites: \\n    ", "similarity_score": 1.3696717023849487}, {"course_title": "DIGITAL IMAGE PROCESSING", "course_code": "ELEN E4830", "department": "Electrical Engineering", "department_code": "ELEN", "points": "3", "instructor": "Christine P Hendon", "scheduled_time_start": 610, "scheduled_time_end": 760, "scheduled_days": "W", "type": "LECTURE", "content": "DIGITAL IMAGE PROCESSING (ELEN E4830)\\n        Course Subtitle: \\n        Description: Introduction to the mathematical tools and algorithmic implementation for representation and processing of digital pictures, videos, and visual sensory data. Image representation, filtering, transform, quality enhancement, restoration, feature extraction, object segmentation, motion analysis, classification, and coding for data compression. A series of programming assignments reinforces material from the lecture...", "similarity_score": 1.3762567043304443}, {"course_title": "TOPICS IN SIGNAL PROCESSING", "course_code": "ELEN E6883", "department": "Electrical Engineering", "department_code": "ELEN", "points": "3", "instructor": "", "scheduled_time_start": 490, "scheduled_time_end": 600, "scheduled_days": "F", "type": "LECTURE", "content": "TOPICS IN SIGNAL PROCESSING (ELEN E6883)\\n        Course Subtitle: INTRO TO BLOCKCHAIN TECH\\n        Description: Advanced topics in signal processing, such as multidimensional signal processing, image feature extraction, image/video editing and indexing, advanced digital filter design, multirate signal processing, adaptive signal processing, and wave-form coding of signals. Content varies from year to year, and different topics rotate through the course numbers 6880 to 6889.\\n        Prerequisites...", "similarity_score": 1.3977580070495605}, {"course_title": "ELECTRONIC CIRCUITS", "course_code": "ELEN E3331", "department": "Electrical Engineering", "department_code": "ELEN", "points": "3", "instructor": "David G Vallancourt", "scheduled_time_start": 700, "scheduled_time_end": 775, "scheduled_days": "MW", "type": "LECTURE", "content": "ELECTRONIC CIRCUITS (ELEN E3331)\\n        Course Subtitle: \\n        Description: Operational amplifier circuits. Diodes and diode circuits. MOS and bipolar junction transistors. Biasing techniques. Small-signal models. Single-stage transistor amplifiers. Analysis and design of CMOS logic gates. A/D and D/A converters.\\n        Prerequisites: \\n    ", "similarity_score": 1.430568814277649}], "total_count": 10}', name='search_courses', id='d82003c1-3c4c-4ece-8ee2-0fd87311acc3', tool_call_id='toolu_01HtkJSS6qwH1H4JnY3GHkeB')]}}}, 'parent_ids': []}

