{'event': 'on_chain_stream', 'run_id': '019b9093-c32e-71a2-8605-55779bfab76c', 'name': 'LangGraph', 'tags': [], 'metadata': {'thread_id': '2de77b04-7c32-47ec-84dc-81f3861507d4'}, 'data': {'chunk': {'tools': {'messages': [ToolMessage(content='{"courses": [{"course_title": "HARDWARE SECURITY", "course_code": "COMS E6424", "department": "Computer Science", "department_code": "COMS", "points": "3", "instructor": "Simha Sethumadhavan", "scheduled_time_start": 610, "scheduled_time_end": 685, "scheduled_days": "MW", "type": "LECTURE", "content": "HARDWARE SECURITY (COMS E6424)\\n        Course Subtitle: \\n        Description: \\n        Prerequisites: \\n    ", "similarity_score": 1.003864049911499}, {"course_title": "OPERATING SYSTEMS I", "course_code": "COMS W4118", "department": "Computer Science", "department_code": "COMS", "points": "3", "instructor": "Kostis Kaffes", "scheduled_time_start": 250, "scheduled_time_end": 325, "scheduled_days": "TR", "type": "LECTURE", "content": "OPERATING SYSTEMS I (COMS W4118)\\n        Course Subtitle: \\n        Description: Design and implementation of operating systems. Topics include process management, process synchronization and interprocess communication, memory management, virtual memory, interrupt handling, processor scheduling, device management, I/O, and file systems. Case study of the UNIX operating system. A programming project is required.\\n        Prerequisites: \\n    ", "similarity_score": 1.0866665840148926}, {"course_title": "DATA STRUCTURES IN JAVA", "course_code": "COMS W3134", "department": "Computer Science", "department_code": "COMS", "points": "3", "instructor": "Paul S Blaer", "scheduled_time_start": 160, "scheduled_time_end": 235, "scheduled_days": "MW", "type": "LECTURE", "content": "DATA STRUCTURES IN JAVA (COMS W3134)\\n        Course Subtitle: \\n        Description: Data types and structures: arrays, stacks, singly and doubly linked lists, queues, trees, sets, and graphs. Programming techniques for processing such structures: sorting and searching, hashing, garbage collection. Storage management. Rudiments of the analysis of algorithms. Taught in Java. Note: Due to significant overlap, students may receive credit for only one of the following three courses: COMS W3134, COMS ...", "similarity_score": 1.2814266681671143}, {"course_title": "USER INTERFACE DESIGN", "course_code": "COMS W4170", "department": "Computer Science", "department_code": "COMS", "points": "3", "instructor": "Lydia Chilton", "scheduled_time_start": 70, "scheduled_time_end": 145, "scheduled_days": "MW", "type": "LECTURE", "content": "USER INTERFACE DESIGN (COMS W4170)\\n        Course Subtitle: \\n        Description: Introduction to the theory and practice of computer user interface design, emphasizing the software design of graphical user interfaces. Topics include basic interaction devices and techniques, human factors, interaction styles, dialogue design, and software infrastructure. Design and programming projects are required.\\n        Prerequisites: \\n    ", "similarity_score": 1.2846137285232544}, {"course_title": "TOPICS IN COMPUTER SCIENCE", "course_code": "COMS W4995", "department": "Computer Science", "department_code": "COMS", "points": "3", "instructor": "Jae W Lee", "scheduled_time_start": 160, "scheduled_time_end": 235, "scheduled_days": "MW", "type": "LECTURE", "content": "TOPICS IN COMPUTER SCIENCE (COMS W4995)\\n        Course Subtitle: ADV SYSTEMS PROGRAMMING\\n        Description: Selected topics in computer science. Content and prerequisites vary between sections and semesters.\xa0May be repeated for credit. Check “topics course” webpage on the department website for more information on each section.\\n        Prerequisites: \\n    ", "similarity_score": 1.2899118661880493}, {"course_title": "ADVANCED PROGRAMMING", "course_code": "COMS W3157", "department": "Computer Science", "department_code": "COMS", "points": "4", "instructor": "Brian Borowski", "scheduled_time_star