{'event': 'on_chat_model_start', 'data': {'input': {'messages': [[SystemMessage(content=[{'type': 'text', 'text': 'You are an expert Columbia University course advisor.\nUse the user profile when answering. \nIf you recommend a class, make sure to check that the user satisfies prerequisites. \nIf a user asks to plan ONLY the next semester, include a timetable where each course has a time slot. \nIf a user asks to plan all of their semesters, do not include times of classes. Include only a list of classes per semester in a table. \n\nIf you are searching up a specific course (to see its timing or prerequisites), use the lookup_course tool. \n- Example: to find information about ELEN E1201 -> lookup_course\n- Example: to find optimization classes that are computational -> search_courses\n\nIf a users current semester is 4, they have 5 semesters remaining. Assume each user graduates in 8 semesters unless stated otherwise.'}, {'type': 'text', 'text': "\n\n## `write_todos`\n\nYou have access to the `write_todos` tool to help you manage and plan complex objectives.\nUse this tool for complex objectives to ensure that you are tracking each necessary step and giving the user visibility into your progress.\nThis tool is very helpful for planning complex objectives, and for breaking down these larger complex objectives into smaller steps.\n\nIt is critical that you mark todos as completed as soon as you are done with a step. Do not batch up multiple steps before marking them as completed.\nFor simple objectives that only require a few steps, it is better to just complete the objective directly and NOT use this tool.\nWriting todos takes time and tokens, use it when it is helpful for managing complex many-step problems! But not for simple few-step requests.\n\n## Important To-Do List Usage Notes to Remember\n- The `write_todos` tool should never be called multiple times in parallel.\n- Don't be afraid to revise the To-Do list as you go. New information may reveal new tasks that need to be done, or old tasks that are irrelevant."}], additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}), HumanMessage(content='tell me what classes to take in 8 semesters as an ee major. i want to be an FPGA engineer at a HFT firm', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='6e5a3997-8e07-45d3-87ca-b96b3a8f9fe2'), AIMessage(content=[{'id': 'toolu_01QEehPsf8c6p8No8UrgsUUw', 'input': {}, 'name': 'get_user_profile', 'type': 'tool_use', 'index': 0, 'partial_json': ''}, {'id': 'toolu_01EPsprkHTCfLKvnEC6QeTud', 'input': {}, 'name': 'lookup_major', 'type': 'tool_use', 'index': 1, 'partial_json': '{"major": "electrical engineering"}'}, {'id': 'toolu_01LNYHkspFNRKAeMAtWYpm1e', 'input': {}, 'name': 'lookup_school_wide_requirements', 'type': 'tool_use', 'index': 2, 'partial_json': '{"input": {"query":"nontechnical_requirements"}}'}, {'id': 'toolu_013k4uoY3JddS6cU97qZwqR3', 'input': {}, 'name': 'lookup_school_wide_requirements', 'type': 'tool_use', 'index': 3, 'partial_json': '{"input": {"query":"technical_requirements"}}'}], additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={'model_name': 'claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929', 'model_provider': 'anthropic', 'stop_reason': 'tool_use', 'stop_sequence': None}, id='lc_run--019b9093-c368-7a71-80ef-25cebc022f84', tool_calls=[{'name': 'get_user_profile', 'args': {}, 'id': 'toolu_01QEehPsf8c6p8No8UrgsUUw', 'type': 'tool_call'}, {'name': 'lookup_major', 'args': {'major': 'electrical engineering'}, 'id': 'toolu_01EPsprkHTCfLKvnEC6QeTud', 'type': 'tool_call'}, {'name': 'lookup_school_wide_requirements', 'args': {'input': {'query': 'nontechnical_requirements'}}, 'id': 'toolu_01LNYHkspFNRKAeMAtWYpm1e', 'type': 'tool_call'}, {'name': 'lookup_school_wide_requirements', 'args': {'input': {'query': 'technical_requirements'}}, 'id': 'toolu_013k4uoY3JddS6cU97qZwqR3', 'type': 'tool_call'}], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 2551, 'output_tokens': 172, 'total_tokens': 2723, 'input_token_details': {'cache_creation': 0, 'cache_read': 0}}), ToolMessage(content='**USER PROFILE**\n    ID: nl2951@columbia.edu\n    Name: None\n    School: None\n    Major: None (None)\n    Semester: None/8\n    Completed: []\n    Goals: []\n    Preferences: []', name='get_user_profile', id='7bd209c8-2d75-49cb-b5fc-96e3dbf3f5f7', tool_call_id='toolu_01QEehPsf8c6p8No8UrgsUUw'), ToolMessage(content="Major requirements for 'electrical engineering':\n{'total_points': 128, 'degree_type': 'BS', 'core_courses': {'intro': ['ELEN E1201'], 'circuits': ['ELEN E3201', 'ELEN E3331'], 'signals_systems': ['ELEN E3801'], 'electromagnetics': ['ELEN E3401'], 'communications_or_networking': ['ELEN E3701', 'CSEE W4119'], 'computer_systems': ['CSEE W3827'], 'professional_practice': ['ELEN E3399'], 'senior_design': ['ELEN E3390']}, 'labs': {'required': ['ELEN E3081', 'ELEN E3084', 'ELEN E3083', 'ELEN E3082', 'ELEN E3043'], 'notes': 'Take labs with corresponding lecture courses when possible'}, 'math_science': {'calculus': ['MATH UN1101', 'MATH UN1102'], 'multivariable': ['APMA E2000', 'APMA E2001'], 'differential_equations': {'default': ['APMA E2101'], 'alternative': ['MATH UN2030', 'APMA E3101 or MATH UN2010']}, 'probability': {'choose_one': ['IEOR E3658', 'STAT GU4203'], 'notes': 'STAT GU4001 / SIEO W3600 generally not accepted as substitutes'}, 'physics': {'choose_one_sequence': {'sequence_1': ['PHYS UN1401', 'PHYS UN1402', 'PHYS UN1403'], 'sequence_2': ['PHYS UN1601', 'PHYS UN1602', 'PHYS UN2601'], 'sequence_3': ['PHYS UN2801', 'PHYS UN2802', 'PHYS UN3081']}, 'lab': {'default': ['PHYS UN1494'], 'substitution_note': 'CHEM UN1500 may substitute for physics lab (not generally recommended)', 'substitute': ['CHEM UN1500']}}, 'chemistry': {'lecture_choose_one': ['CHEM UN1403', 'CHEM UN1404', 'CHEM UN2045', 'CHEM UN1604']}, 'computer_science': {'data_structures_choose_one': ['COMS W3134', 'COMS W3136', 'COMS W3137'], 'notes': 'If planning a CS minor, prefer COMS W3134 or COMS W3137'}}, 'technical_electives': {'total_points': 18, 'constraints': {'ee_courses_must_be_3000_level_or_above': True, 'no_significant_overlap': True, 'advisor_approval_if_not_clearly_listed': True}, 'depth': {'points': 6, 'requirement': '>=6 points of EE courses in ONE chosen depth area', 'areas': ['photonics, solid-state devices, and electromagnetics', 'circuits and electronics', 'signals and systems', 'communications and networking']}, 'breadth': {'points': 6, 'requirement': '>=6 points OUTSIDE chosen depth area with significant engineering content'}, 'other': {'points': 6, 'requirement': 'Any additional technical courses to reach 18 total (engineering not required unless missing ELEN E1201)'}}, 'nontechnical': {'total_points': 27, 'required': {'university_writing': ['ENGL CC1010'], 'core_humanities_sequence_choose_one': {'literature_humanities': ['HUMA CC1001', 'HUMA CC1002'], 'contemporary_civilization': ['COCI CC1101', 'COCI CC1102'], 'global_core': 'Two approved Global Core courses (letter grade)'}, 'art_or_music_choose_one': ['HUMA UN1121', 'HUMA UN1123'], 'economics': ['ECON UN1105']}, 'electives': {'points': '9–11', 'rule': 'Choose from SEAS-approved nontechnical elective list (List B); cannot be modified by advisors'}, 'notes': 'Required nontechnical courses are 16–18 points (List A) + 9–11 elective points (List B) = at least 27 total'}, 'other_requirements': {'art_of_engineering': ['ENGI E1102'], 'physical_education': ['PHED UN1001', 'PHED UN1002']}, 'notes': {'early_start': 'ELEN E1201 can be taken as early as first year (typically spring)', 'transfer_students': {'plan_1': 'No ELEN E1201 equivalent — cannot choose circuits & electronics as depth area', 'plan_2': 'Has ELEN E1201 equivalent — can choose circuits & electronics as depth area'}, 'technical_elective_waiver': {'condition': 'If APMA E2101 replaced by MATH UN2030 + Linear Algebra', 'effect': 'Technical electives reduced from 18 to 15 points'}}}\nSource: [220, 221, 222, 223, 224, 225, 226]\n", name='lookup_major', id='a6279e26-946e-470f-a352-d45900af4b80', tool_call_id='toolu_01EPsprkHTCfLKvnEC6QeTud'), ToolMessage(content='{"total_points_required": 27, "lists": {"A_required_nontechnical": {"points_required": {"min": 16, "max": 18}, "rules": ["Must be taken at Columbia.", "All components are required for Engineering students.", "Neither List A nor List B may be modified by advisers."], "components": {"university_writing": ["ENGL CC1010"], "literature_or_civilization_sequence": {"choose_one": [{"id": "literature_humanities", "courses": ["HUMA CC1001", "HUMA CC1002"], "points": 6}, {"id": "contemporary_civilization", "courses": ["COCI CC1101", "COCI CC1102"], "points": 6}, {"id": "global_core_substitution", "rule": "Two approved Global Core courses taken for a letter grade.", "points": {"min": 6, "max": 8}}]}, "art_or_music_humanities": {"choose_one": ["HUMA UN1121", "HUMA UN1123"]}, "principles_of_economics": {"course": "ECON UN1105", "notes": ["May be satisfied through AP credit.", "Barnard substitutes are not permitted."]}}}, "B_elective_nontechnical": {"points_required": {"min": 9, "max": 11}, "rules": ["Must be chosen from the approved List B departmental rules.", "Professional/workshop/lab/project/scientific/studio/music-instruction/master’s-level professional courses do not count.", "AP credit in appropriate subject areas may apply toward the elective nontechnical requirement."], "departmental_rules_reference": "course_eligibility_rules"}}}', name='lookup_school_wide_requirements', id='1cc5dd0c-94d7-417f-9cab-ee34599df59c', tool_call_id='toolu_01LNYHkspFNRKAeMAtWYpm1e'), ToolMessage(content='{"required_course": ["ENGI E1102"], "technical_areas": ["engineering", "mathematics", "physics", "chemistry", "computer_science"], "notes": ["ENGI E1102 (The Art of Engineering) is required of all first-year Engineering students.", "Departments may recommend or require certain technical courses earlier for efficiency."]}', name='lookup_school_wide_requirements', id='4adb4b5c-ac6c-4e51-93b6-9aa130ffeb21', tool_call_id='toolu_013k4uoY3JddS6cU97qZwqR3'), AIMessage(content=[{'text': 'Now let me search for courses that are particularly relevant for an FPGA engineer at an HFT (High-Frequency Trading) firm:', 'type': 'text', 'index': 0}, {'id': 'toolu_01HtkJSS6qwH1H4JnY3GHkeB', 'input': {}, 'name': 'search_courses', 'type': 'tool_use', 'index': 1, 'partial_json': '{"input": {"query":"FPGA digital design hardware","limit":10}}'}, {'id': 'toolu_01NvK2V6C5BicRkPURSVqVKj', 'input': {}, 'name': 'search_courses', 'type': 'tool_use', 'index': 2, 'partial_json': '{"input": {"query":"VHDL Verilog hardware description language","limit":10}}'}, {'id': 'toolu_017F3sbvzDamdNj65f6D8WUC', 'input': {}, 'name': 'search_courses', 'type': 'tool_use', 'index': 3, 'partial_json': '{"input": {"query":"computer architecture hardware systems","limit":10}}'}, {'id': 'toolu_01CyLVgygtsCe1T8D8b3LZpZ', 'input': {}, 'name': 'search_courses', 'type': 'tool_use', 'index': 4, 'partial_json': '{"input": {"query":"high performance computing parallel processing","limit":10}}'}, {'id': 'toolu_01HE6nFTu5eSdwpYhGCMc6fr', 'input': {}, 'name': 'search_courses', 'type': 'tool_use', 'index': 5, 'partial_json': '{"input": {"query":"algorithms data structures optimization","limit":10}}'}], additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={'model_name': 'claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929', 'model_provider': 'anthropic', 'stop_reason': 'tool_use', 'stop_sequence': None}, id='lc_run--019b9093-d229-7831-baff-6dc0aac3046e', tool_calls=[{'name': 'search_courses', 'args': {'input': {'query': 'FPGA digital design hardware', 'limit': 10}}, 'id': 'toolu_01HtkJSS6qwH1H4JnY3GHkeB', 'type': 'tool_call'}, {'name': 'search_courses', 'args': {'input': {'query': 'VHDL Verilog hardware description language', 'limit': 10}}, 'id': 'toolu_01NvK2V6C5BicRkPURSVqVKj', 'type': 'tool_call'}, {'name': 'search_courses', 'args': {'input': {'query': 'computer architecture hardware systems', 'limit': 10}}, 'id': 'toolu_017F3sbvzDamdNj65f6D8WUC', 'type': 'tool_call'}, {'name': 'search_courses', 'args': {'input': {'query': 'high performance computing parallel processing', 'limit': 10}}, 'id': 'toolu_01CyLVgygtsCe1T8D8b3LZpZ', 'type': 'tool_call'}, {'name': 'search_courses', 'args': {'input': {'query': 'algorithms data structures optimization', 'limit': 10}}, 'id': 'toolu_01HE6nFTu5eSdwpYhGCMc6fr', 'type': 'tool_call'}], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 4691, 'output_tokens': 303, 'total_tokens': 4994, 'input_token_details': {'cache_creation': 0, 'cache_read': 0}}), ToolMessage(content='{"courses": [{"course_title": "Analog-Digital Interfaces in VLSI", "course_code": "ELEN E6316", "department": "Electrical Engineering", "department_code": "ELEN", "points": "3", "instructor": "Timothy Dickson", "scheduled_time_start": 420, "scheduled_time_end": 570, "scheduled_days": "T", "type": "LECTURE", "content": "Analog-Digital Interfaces in VLSI (ELEN E6316)\\n        Course Subtitle: Analog-Digital Interfaces\\n        Description: Analog-to-digital and digital-to-analog conversion techniques for very large scale integrated circuits and systems. Precision sampling; quantization; A/D and D/A converter architectures and metrics; Nyquist architectures; oversampling architectures; correction techniques; system considerations. A design project is an integral part of this course.\\n        Prerequisites: \\n    ", "similarity_score": 1.1390514373779297}, {"course_title": "VLSI DESIGN LABORATORY", "course_code": "ELEN E6350", "department": "Electrical Engineering", "department_code": "ELEN", "points": "3", "instructor": "Mingoo Seok", "scheduled_time_start": 880, "scheduled_time_end": 955, "scheduled_days": "TR", "type": "LABORATORY", "content": "VLSI DESIGN LABORATORY (ELEN E6350)\\n        Course Subtitle: \\n        Description: Design of a CMOS mixed-signal integrated circuit. The class divides up into teams to work on mixed-signal integrated circuit designs. The chips are fabricated to be tested the following term. Lectures cover use of computer-aided design tools, design issues specific to the projects, and chip integration issues. This course shares lectures with E4350, but the complexity requirements of integrated circuits are higher...", "similarity_score": 1.2171201705932617}, {"course_title": "PHOTONIC INTEGRATED CIRCUITS", "course_code": "ELEN E6414", "department": "Electrical Engineering", "department_code": "ELEN", "points": "3", "instructor": "Michal Lipson", "scheduled_time_start": 970, "scheduled_time_end": 1120, "scheduled_days": "W", "type": "LECTURE", "content": "PHOTONIC INTEGRATED CIRCUITS (ELEN E6414)\\n        Course Subtitle: PHOTONIC INTEGRATED CIRCU\\n        Description: Photonic integrated circuits are important subsystem components for telecommunications, optically controlled radar, optical signal processing, and photonic local area networks. An introduction to the devices and the design of these circuits. Principle and modeling of dielectric waveguides (including silica on silicon and InP based materials), waveguide devices (simple and star couple...", "similarity_score": 1.2714366912841797}, {"course_title": "DIGITAL SYSTEMS LABORATORY", "course_code": "ELEN E3082", "department": "Electrical Engineering", "department_code": "ELEN", "points": "1", "instructor": "Kenneth Shepard", "scheduled_time_start": 250, "scheduled_time_end": 400, "scheduled_days": "M", "type": "LABORATORY", "content": "DIGITAL SYSTEMS LABORATORY (ELEN E3082)\\n        Course Subtitle: DIGITAL SYSTEMS LABORATOR\\n        Description: Companion lab course for CSEE W3827. Experiments cover such topics as logic gates; flip-flops; shift registers; counters; combinational logic circuits; sequential logic circuits; programmable logic devices. The lab generally meets on alternate weeks.\\n        Prerequisites: CSEE W3827\\n    ", "similarity_score": 1.3084306716918945}, {"course_title": "COMMUNICATION CIRCUITS", "course_code": "ELEN E4314", "department": "Electrical Engineering", "department_code": "ELEN", "points": "3", "instructor": "Emily Naviasky", "scheduled_time_start": 250, "scheduled_time_end": 400, "scheduled_days": "R", "type": "LECTURE", "content": "COMMUNICATION CIRCUITS (ELEN E4314)\\n        Course Subtitle: \\n        Description: Principles of electronic circuits used in the generation, transmission, and reception of signal waveforms, as used in analog and digital communication systems. Nonlinearity and distortion; power amplifiers; tuned amplifiers; oscillators; multipliers and mixers; modulators and demodulators; phase-locked loops. An extensive design project is an integral part of the course.\\n        Prerequisites: \\n    ", "similarity_score": 1.3107632398605347}, {"course_title": "ADV ANALOG INTEGRATED CIRCUITS", "course_code": "ELEN E6312", "department": "Electrical Engineering", "department_code": "ELEN", "points": "3", "instructor": "Harish Krishnaswamy", "scheduled_time_start": 250, "scheduled_time_end": 400, "scheduled_days": "T", "type": "LECTURE", "content": "ADV ANALOG INTEGRATED CIRCUITS (ELEN E6312)\\n        Course Subtitle: ADV ANALOG INTEGRATED CIR\\n        Description: Integrated circuit device characteristics and models; temperature- and supply-independent biasing; IC operational amplifier analysis and design and their applications; feedback amplifiers, stability and frequency compensation techniques; noise in circuits and low-noise design; mismatch in circuits and low-offset design. Computer-aided analysis techniques are used in homework(s) or ...", "similarity_score": 1.3218504190444946}, {"course_title": "DIGITAL COMMUNICATIONS", "course_code": "ELEN E4702", "department": "Electrical Engineering", "department_code": "ELEN", "points": "3", "instructor": "Alexei Ashikhmin", "scheduled_time_start": 420, "scheduled_time_end": 570, "scheduled_days": "W", "type": "LECTURE", "content": "DIGITAL COMMUNICATIONS (ELEN E4702)\\n        Course Subtitle: \\n        Description: Digital communications for both point-to-point and switched applications is further developed. Optimum receiver structures and transmitter signal shaping for both binary and M-ary signal transmission. An introduction to block codes and convolutional codes, with application to space communications.\\n        Prerequisites: \\n    ", "similarity_score": 1.3696717023849487}, {"course_title": "DIGITAL IMAGE PROCESSING", "course_code": "ELEN E4830", "department": "Electrical Engineering", "department_code": "ELEN", "points": "3", "instructor": "Christine P Hendon", "scheduled_time_start": 610, "scheduled_time_end": 760, "scheduled_days": "W", "type": "LECTURE", "content": "DIGITAL IMAGE PROCESSING (ELEN E4830)\\n        Course Subtitle: \\n        Description: Introduction to the mathematical tools and algorithmic implementation for representation and processing of digital pictures, videos, and visual sensory data. Image representation, filtering, transform, quality enhancement, restoration, feature extraction, object segmentation, motion analysis, classification, and coding for data compression. A series of programming assignments reinforces material from the lecture...", "similarity_score": 1.3762567043304443}, {"course_title": "TOPICS IN SIGNAL PROCESSING", "course_code": "ELEN E6883", "department": "Electrical Engineering", "department_code": "ELEN", "points": "3", "instructor": "", "scheduled_time_start": 490, "scheduled_time_end": 600, "scheduled_days": "F", "type": "LECTURE", "content": "TOPICS IN SIGNAL PROCESSING (ELEN E6883)\\n        Course Subtitle: INTRO TO BLOCKCHAIN TECH\\n        Description: Advanced topics in signal processing, such as multidimensional signal processing, image feature extraction, image/video editing and indexing, advanced digital filter design, multirate signal processing, adaptive signal processing, and wave-form coding of signals. Content varies from year to year, and different topics rotate through the course numbers 6880 to 6889.\\n        Prerequisites...", "similarity_score": 1.3977580070495605}, {"course_title": "ELECTRONIC CIRCUITS", "course_code": "E