ORATORY", "course_code": "ELEN E6350", "department": "Electrical Engineering", "department_code": "ELEN", "points": "3", "instructor": "Mingoo Seok", "scheduled_time_start": 880, "scheduled_time_end": 955, "scheduled_days": "TR", "type": "LABORATORY", "content": "VLSI DESIGN LABORATORY (ELEN E6350)\\n        Course Subtitle: \\n        Description: Design of a CMOS mixed-signal integrated circuit. The class divides up into teams to work on mixed-signal integrated circuit designs. The chips are fabricated to be tested the following term. Lectures cover use of computer-aided design tools, design issues specific to the projects, and chip integration issues. This course shares lectures with E4350, but the complexity requirements of integrated circuits are higher...", "similarity_score": 1.2171201705932617}, {"course_title": "PHOTONIC INTEGRATED CIRCUITS", "course_code": "ELEN E6414", "department": "Electrical Engineering", "department_code": "ELEN", "points": "3", "instructor": "Michal Lipson", "scheduled_time_start": 970, "scheduled_time_end": 1120, "scheduled_days": "W", "type": "LECTURE", "content": "PHOTONIC INTEGRATED CIRCUITS (ELEN E6414)\\n        Course Subtitle: PHOTONIC INTEGRATED CIRCU\\n        Description: Photonic integrated circuits are important subsystem components for telecommunications, optically controlled radar, optical signal processing, and photonic local area networks. An introduction to the devices and the design of these circuits. Principle and modeling of dielectric waveguides (including silica on silicon and InP based materials), waveguide devices (simple and star couple...", "similarity_score": 1.2714366912841797}, {"course_title": "DIGITAL SYSTEMS LABORATORY", "course_code": "ELEN E3082", "department": "Electrical Engineering", "department_code": "ELEN", "points": "1", "instructor": "Kenneth Shepard", "scheduled_time_start": 250, "scheduled_time_end": 400, "scheduled_days": "M", "type": "LABORATORY", "content": "DIGITAL SYSTEMS LABORATORY (