rty'}, 'parent_ids': ['019b9093-c32e-71a2-8605-55779bfab76c', '019b9094-310a-7c40-b114-ea09cbc3958d']}
{'event': 'on_chain_stream', 'run_id': '019b9094-310a-7c40-b114-ea09cbc3958d', 'name': 'model', 'tags': ['graph:step:24'], 'metadata': {'thread_id': '2de77b04-7c32-47ec-84dc-81f3861507d4', 'langgraph_step': 24, 'langgraph_node': 'model', 'langgraph_triggers': ('branch:to:model',), 'langgraph_path': ('__pregel_pull', 'model'), 'langgraph_checkpoint_ns': 'model:1b672164-0501-8c25-c35b-8c8411d376b1'}, 'data': {'chunk': {'messages': [AIMessage(content=[{'text': "Based on the requirements and your goal to become an FPGA engineer at an HFT firm, I'll create a comprehensive 8-semester plan. As an FPGA engineer in high-frequency trading, you'll need strong foundations in:\n- Digital design and hardware description languages (VHDL/Verilog)\n- Computer architecture and systems\n- High-performance computing\n- Low-latency systems and networking\n- Algorithms and data structures\n- Some finance background\n\nHere's your recommended **8-semester plan as an Electrical Engineering major**:\n\n## **Semester 1 (Fall, First Year)**\n| Course Code | Course Title | Points | Notes |\n|------------|--------------|---------|--------|\n| ENGI E1102 | Art of Engineering | 3 | Required for all SEAS students |\n| MATH UN1101 | Calculus I | 3 | Math/Science requirement |\n| PHYS UN1401 | Physics I (Mechanics) | 3 | Physics sequence |\n| CHEM UN1403 | General Chemistry I | 3 | Chemistry requirement |\n| ENGL CC1010 | University Writing | 3 | Nontechnical requirement |\n| PHED UN1001 | Physical Education | 0 | PE requirement |\n| **Total** | | **15** | |\n\n## **Semester 2 (Spring, First Year)**\n| Course Code | Course Title | Points | Notes |\n|------------|--------------|---------|--------|\n| ELEN E1201 | Introduction to Electrical Engineering | 3 | EE core intro course |\n| MATH UN1102 | Calculus II | 3 | Math/Science requirement |\n| PHYS UN1402 | Physics II (E&M) | 3 | Physics sequence |\n| PHYS UN1494 | Physics Lab | 1 | Physics lab requirement |\n| HUMA CC1001 | Literature Humanities I | 3 | Nontechnical requirement |\n| PHED UN1002 | Physical Education | 0 | PE requirement |\n| **Total** | | **13** | |\n\n## **Semester 3 (Fall, Second Year)**\n| Course Code | Course Title | Points | Notes |\n|------------|--------------|---------|--------|\n| ELEN E3201 | Circuit Analysis | 3 | EE core circuits |\n| ELEN E3081 | Circuits Lab | 1 | Required lab |\n| APMA E2000 | Multivariable Calculus | 3 | Math/Science requirement |\n| PHYS UN1403 | Physics III (Waves/Optics) | 3 | Physics sequence |\n| COMS W3134 | Data Structures in Java | 3 | CS requirement - crucial for HFT |\n| HUMA CC1002 | Literature Humanities II | 3 | Nontechnical requirement |\n| **Total** | | **16** | |\n\n## **Semester 4 (Spring, Second Year)**\n| Course Code | Course Title | Points | Notes |\n|------------|--------------|---------|--------|\n| ELEN E3331 | Electronic Circuits | 3 | EE core circuits |\n| ELEN E3084 | Electronics Lab | 1 | Required lab |\n| CSEE W3827 | Fundamentals of Computer Systems | 3 | EE core - **CRITICAL for FPGA** |\n| ELEN E3082 | Digital Systems Lab | 1 | Required lab - **CRITICAL for FPGA** |\n| APMA E2001 | Multivariable Calculus II | 3 | Math/Science requirement |\n| ECON UN1105 | Principles of Economics | 3 | Nontechnical requirement |\n| **Total** | | **14** | |\n\n## **Semester 5 (Fall, Third Year)**\n| Course Code | Course Title | Points | Notes |\n|------------|--------------|---------|--------|\n| ELEN E3401 | Electromagnetics | 3 | EE core |\n| ELEN E3043 | Electromagnetics Lab | 1 | Required lab |\n| ELEN E3801 | Signals and Systems | 3 | EE core |\n| ELEN E3083 | Signals & Systems Lab | 1 | Required lab |\n| APMA E2101 | ODEs & Linear Algebra | 4 | Math/Science requirement |\n| COMS W3157 | Advanced Programming (C/Unix) | 4 | **CRITICAL for HFT - low-level programming** |\n| **Total** | | **16** | |\n\n## **Semester 6 (Spring, Third Year)**\n| Course Code | Course Title | Points | Notes |\n|------------|--------------|---------|--------|\n| ELEN E3399 | Professional Practice | 0 | EE core requirement |\n| CSEE W4119 | Computer Networks | 3 | EE core - **Important for HFT networking** |\n| IEOR E3658 | Probability & Statistics | 3 | Math/Science requirement |\n| ELEN E4350 | VLSI Design Laboratory | 3 | **CRITICAL - FPGA design experience** |\n| COMS W4232 | Advanced Algorithms | 3 | **CRITICAL for HFT - optimization** |\n| HUMA UN1121 or UN1123 | Art/Music Humanities | 3 | Nontechnical requirement |\n| **Total** | | **15** | |\n\n## **Semester 7 (Fall, Fourth Year)**\n| Course Code | Course Title | Points | Notes |\n|------------|--------------|---------|--------|\n| ELEN E3390 | Senior Design I | 3 | EE core capstone |\n| COMS W4118 | Operating Systems | 3 | **Important for systems understanding** |\n| ELEN E4314 | Communication Circuits | 3 | Depth elective (Circuits area) - high-speed circuits |\n| COMS E6424 | Hardware Security | 3 | Breadth elective - FPGA security |\n| Nontechnical Elective | List B Elective | 3 | Nontechnical elective |\n| **Total** | | **15** | |\n\n## **Semester 8 (Spring, Fourth Year)**\n| Course Code | Course Title | Points | Notes |\n|------------|--------------|---------|--------|\n| ELEN E3390 | Senior Design II | 0 | EE core capstone continuation |\n| ELEN E6316 | Analog-Digital Interfaces in VLSI | 3 | Technical elective - ADC/DAC for trading systems |\n| ELEN E4702 | Digital Communications | 3 | Technical elective - high-speed data |\n| Nontechnical Elective | List B Elective | 3 | Nontechnical elective |\n| Nontechnical Elective | List B Elective | 3 | Nontechnical elective |\n| **Total** | | **12** | |\n\n---\n\n## **Summary & Key Points:**\n\n**Total Points: ~131** (exceeds 128 minimum)\n\n### **Why This Plan is Perfect for FPGA Engineering at HFT:**\n\n1. **Digital Design Foundation:**\n   - CSEE W3827 (Computer Systems) + ELEN E3082 (Digital Systems Lab) - You'll learn digital logic, state machines, and hardware design\n   - ELEN E4350 (VLSI Design Lab) - Hands-on FPGA/ASIC design with CAD tools\n\n2. **Low-Level Programming (Critical for HFT):**\n   - COMS W3157 (Advanced Programming) - C programming, Unix, TCP/IP networking\n   - COMS W3134 (Data Structures) - Efficient algorithms\n   - COMS W4232 (Advanced Algorithms) - Optimization techniques used in HFT\n\n3. **High-Performance Systems:**\n   - COMS W4118 (Operating Systems) - Understanding of scheduling, memory management\n   - CSEE W4119 (Computer Networks) - Low-latency networking\n\n4. **Hardware-Software Interface:**\n   - ELEN E6316 (Analog-Digital Interfaces) - ADC/DAC crucial for market data feeds\n   - ELEN E4314 (Communication Circuits) - High-speed circuit design\n   - COMS E6424 (Hardware Security) - FPGA security considerations\n\n5. **Signals & Communications:**\n   - ELEN E3801 (Signals and Systems) - Signal processing fundamentals\n   - ELEN E4702 (Digital Communications) - High-speed data transmission\n\n### **Career Preparation:**\n- Strong C/C++ programming skills (COMS W3157)\n- FPGA design experience (ELEN E4350, CSEE W3827)\n- Algorithm optimization (COMS W4232)\n- Low-latency networking (CSEE W4119, COMS W3157)\n- Hardware-software co-design experience\n\n### **Recommendations:**\n1. **Summer internships:** Seek FPGA or HFT internships after sophomore/junior years\n2. **Side projects:** Build FPGA projects (maybe implement trading algorithms on FPGA)\n3. **Learn HDLs:** Practice Verilog/VHDL outside of class\n4. **Finance knowledge:** Consider auditing finance courses or self-studying market microstructure\n5. **Programming:** Master C++ as it's the primary language in HFT\n\nThis plan balances all EE requirements while giving you the computer science, algorithms, and systems knowledge that HFT firms seek in FPGA engineers!", 'type': 'text', 'index': 0}], additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={'model_name': 'claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929', 'model_provider': 'anthropic', 'stop_reason': 'end_turn', 'stop_sequence': None}, id='lc_run--019b9094-311f-7781-8b0b-b9d9ce04d6bf', usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 19502, 'output_tokens': 2330, 'total_tokens': 21832, 'input_token_details': {'cache_creation': 0, 'cache_read': 0}})]}}, 'parent_ids': ['019b9093-c32e-71a2-8605-55779bfab76c']}
{'event': 'on_chain_end', 'data': {'output': {'messages': [AIMessage(content=[{'text': "Based on the requirements and your goal to become an FPGA engineer at an HFT firm, I'll create a comprehensive 8-semester plan. As an FPGA engineer in high-frequency trading, you'll need strong foundations in:\n- Digital design and hardware description languages (VHDL/Verilog)\n- Computer architecture and systems\n- High-performance computing\n- Low-latency systems and networking\n- Algorithms and data structures\n- Some finance background\n\nHere's your recommended **8-semester plan as an Electrical Engineering major**:\n\n## **Semester 1 (Fall, First Year)**\n| Course Code | Course Title | Points | Notes |\n|------------|--------------|---------|--------|\n| ENGI E1102 | Art of Engineering | 3 | Required for all SEAS students |\n| MATH UN1101 | Calculus I | 3 | Math/Science requirement |\n| PHYS UN1401 | Physics I (Mechanics) | 3 | Physics sequence |\n| CHEM UN1403 | General Chemistry I | 3 | Chemistry requirement |\n| ENGL CC1010 | University Writing | 3 | Nontechnical requirement |\n| PHED UN1001 | Physical Education | 0 | PE requirement |\n| **Total** | | **15** | |\n\n## **Semester 2 (Spring, First Year)**\n| Course Code | Course Title | Points | Notes |\n|------------|--------------|---------|--------|\n| ELEN E1201 | Introduction to Electrical Engineering | 3 | EE core intro course |\n| MATH UN1102 | Calculus II | 3 | Math/Science requirement |\n| PHYS UN1402 | Physics II (E&M) | 3 | Physics sequence |\n| PHYS UN1494 | Physics Lab | 1 | Physics lab requirement |\n| HUMA CC1001 | Literature Humanities I | 3 | Nontechnical requirement |\n| PHED UN1002 | Physical Education | 0 | PE requirement |\n| **Total** | | **13** | |\n\n## **Semester 3 (Fall, Second Year)**\n| Course Code | Course Title | Points | Notes |\n|------------|--------------|---------|--------|\n| ELEN E3201 | Circuit Analysis | 3 | EE core circuits |\n| ELEN E3081 | Circuits Lab | 1 | Required lab |\n| APMA E2000 | Multivariable Calculus | 3 | Math/Science requirement |\n| PHYS UN1403 | Physics III (Waves/Optics) | 3 | Physics sequence |\n| COMS W3134 | Data Structures in Java | 3 | CS requirement - crucial for HFT |\n| HUMA CC1002 | Literature Humanities II | 3 | Nontechnical requirement |\n| **Total** | | **16** | |\n\n## **Semester 4 (Spring, Second Year)**\n| Course Code | Course Title | Points | Notes |\n|------------|--------------|---------|--------|\n| ELEN E3331 | Electronic Circuits | 3 | EE core circuits |\n| ELEN E3084 | Electronics Lab | 1 | Required lab |\n| CSEE W3827 | Fundamentals of Computer Systems | 3 | EE core - **CRITICAL for FPGA** |\n| ELEN E3082 | Digital Systems Lab | 1 | Required lab - **CRITICAL for FPGA** |\n| APMA E2001 | Multivariable Calculus II | 3 | Math/Science requirement |\n| ECON UN1105 | Principles of Economics | 3 | Nontechnical requirement |\n| **Total** | | **14** | |\n\n## **Semester 5 (Fall, Third Year)**\n| Course Code | Course Title | Points | Notes |\n|------------|--------------|---------|--------|\n| ELEN E3401 | Electromagnetics | 3 | EE core |\n| ELEN E3043 | Electromagnetics Lab | 1 | Required lab |\n| ELEN E3801 | Signals and Systems | 3 | EE core |\n| ELEN E3083 | Signals & Systems Lab | 1 | Required lab |\n| APMA E2101 | ODEs & Linear Algebra | 4 | Math/Science requirement |\n| COMS W3157 | Advanced Programming (C/Unix) | 4 | **CRITICAL for HFT - low-level programming** |\n| **Total** | | **16** | |\n\n## **Semester 6 (Spring, Third Year)**\n| Course Code | Course Title | Points | Notes |\n|------------|--------------|---------|--------|\n| ELEN E3399 | Professional Practice | 0 | EE core requirement |\n| CSEE W4119 | Computer Networks | 3 | EE core - **Important for HFT networking** |\n| IEOR E3658 | Probability & Statistics | 3 | Math/Science requirement |\n| ELEN E4350 | VLSI Design Laboratory | 3 | **CRITICAL - FPGA design experience** |\n| COMS W4232 | Advanced Algorithms | 3 | **CRITICAL for HFT - optimization** |\n| HUMA UN1121 or UN1123 | Art/Music Humanities | 3 | Nontechnical requirement |\n| **Total** | | **15** | |\n\n## **Semester 7 (Fall, Fourth Year)**\n| Course Code | Course Title | Points | Notes |\n|------------|--------------|---------|--------|\n| ELEN E3390 | Senior Design I | 3 | EE core capstone |\n| COMS W4118 | Operating Systems | 3 | **Important for systems understanding** |\n| ELEN E4314 | Communication Circuits | 3 | Depth elective (Circuits area) - high-speed circuits |\n| COMS E6424 | Hardware Security | 3 | Breadth elective - FPGA security |\n| Nontechnical Elective | List B Elective | 3 | Nontechnical elective |\n| **Total** | | **15** | |\n\n## **Semester 8 (Spring, Fourth Year)**\n| Course Code | Course Title | Points | Notes |\n|------------|--------------|---------|--------|\n| ELEN E3390 | Senior Design II | 0 | EE core capstone continuation |\n| ELEN E6316 | Analog-Digital Interfaces in VLSI | 3 | Technical elective - ADC/DAC for trading systems |\n| ELEN E4702 | Digital Communications | 3 | Technical elective - high-speed data |\n| Nontechnical Elective | List B Elective | 3 | Nontechnical elective |\n| Nontechnical Elective | List B Elective | 3 | Nontechnical elective |\n| **Total** | | **12** | |\n\n---\n\n## **Summary & Key Points:**\n\n**Total Points: ~131** (exceeds 128 minimum)\n\n### **Why This Plan is Perfect for FPGA Engineering at HFT:**\n\n1. **Digital Design Foundation:**\n   - CSEE W3827 (Computer Systems) + ELEN E3082 (Digital Systems Lab) - You'll learn digital logic, state machines, and hardware design\n   - ELEN E4350 (VLSI Design Lab) - Hands-on FPGA/ASIC design with CAD tools\n\n2. **Low-Level Programming (Critical for HFT):**\n   - COMS W3157 (Advanced Programming) - C programming, Unix, TCP/IP networking\n   - COMS W3134 (Data Structures) - Efficient algorithms\n   - COMS W4232 (Advanced Algorithms) - Optimization techniques used in HFT\n\n3. **High-Performance Systems:**\n   - COMS W4118 (Operating Systems) - Understanding of scheduling, memory management\n   - CSEE W4119 (Computer Networks) - Low-latency networking\n\n4. **Hardware-Software Interface:**\n   - ELEN E6316 (Analog-Digital Interfaces) - ADC/DAC crucial for market data feeds\n   - ELEN E4314 (Communication Circuits) - High-speed circuit design\n   - COMS E6424 (Hardware Security) - FPGA security considerations\n\n5. **Signals & Communications:**\n   - ELEN E3801 (Signals and Systems) - Signal processing fundamentals\n   - ELEN E4702 (Digital Communications) - High-speed data transmission\n\n### **Career Preparation:**\n- Strong C/C++ programming skills (COMS W3157)\n- FPGA design experience (ELEN E4350, CSEE W3827)\n- Algorithm optimization (COMS W4232)\n- Low-latency networking (CSEE W4119, COMS W3157)\n- Hardware-software co-design experience\n\n### **Recommendations:**\n1. **Summer internships:** Seek FPGA or HFT internships after sophomore/junior years\n2. **Side projects:** Build FPGA projects (maybe implement trading algorithms on FPGA)\n3. **Learn HDLs:** Practice Verilog/VHDL outside of class\n4. **Finance knowledge:** Consider auditing finance courses or self-studying market microstructure\n5. **Programming:** Master C++ as it's the primary language in HFT\n\nThis plan balances all EE requirements while giving you the computer science, algorithms, and systems knowledge that HFT firms seek in FPGA engineers!", 'type': 'text', 'index': 0}], additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={'model_name': 'claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929', 'model_provider': 'anthropic', 'stop_reason': 'end_turn', 'stop_sequence': None}, id='lc_run--019b9094-311f-7781-8b0b-b9d9ce04d6bf', usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 19502, 'output_tokens': 2330, 'total_tokens': 21832, 'input_token_details': {'cache_creation': 0, 'cache_read': 0}})]}, 'input': {'messages': [HumanMessage(content='tell me what classes to take in 8 semesters as an ee major. i want to be an FPGA engineer at a HFT firm', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='6e5a3997-8e07-45d3-87ca-b96b3a8f9fe2'), AIMessage(content=[{'id': 'toolu_01QEehPsf8c6p8No8UrgsUUw', 'input': {}, 'name': 'get_user_profile', 'type': 'tool_use', 'index': 0, 'partial_json': ''}, {'id': 'toolu_01EPsprkHTCfLKvnEC6QeTud', 'input': {}, 'name': 'lookup_major', 'type': 'tool_use', 'index': 1, 'partial_json': '{"major": "electrical engineering"}'}, {'id': 'toolu_01LNYHkspFNRKAeMAtWYpm1e', 'input': {}, 'name': 'lookup_school_wide_requirements', 'type': 'tool_use', 'index': 2, 'partial_json': '{"input": {"query":"nontechnical_requirements"}}'}, {'id': 'toolu_013k4uoY3JddS6cU97qZwqR3', 'input': {}, 'name': 'lookup_school_wide_requirements', 'type': 'tool_use', 'index': 3, 'partial_json': '{"input": {"query":"technical_requirements"}}'}], additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={'model_name': 'claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929', 'model_provider': 'anthropic', 'stop_reason': 'tool_use', 'stop_sequence': None}, id='lc_run--019b9093-c368-7a71-80ef-25cebc022f84', tool_calls=[{'name': 'get_user_profile', 'args': {}, 'id': 'toolu_01QEehPsf8c6p8No8UrgsUUw', 'type': 'tool_call'}, {'name': 'lookup_major', 'args': {'major': 'electrical engineering'}, 'id': 'toolu_01EPsprkHTCfLKvnEC6QeTud', 'type': 'tool_call'}, {'name': 'lookup_school_wide_requirements', 'args': {'input': {'query': 'nontechnical_requirements'}}, 'id': 'toolu_01LNYHkspFNRKAeMAtWYpm1e', 'type': 'tool_call'}, {'name': 'lookup_school_wide_requirements', 'args': {'input': {'query': 'technical_requirements'}}, 'id': 'toolu_013k4uoY3JddS6cU97qZwqR3', 'type': 'tool_call'}], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 2551, 'output_tokens': 172, 'total_tokens': 2723, 'input_token_details': {'cache_creation': 0, 'cache_read': 0}}), ToolMessage(content='**USER PROFILE**\n    ID: nl2951@columbia.edu\n    Name: None\n    School: None\n    Major: None (None)\n    Semester: None/8\n    Completed: []\n    Goals: []\n    Preferences: []', name='get_user_profile', id='7bd209c8-2d75-49cb-b5fc-96e3dbf3f5f7', tool_call_id='toolu_01QEehPsf8c6p8No8UrgsUUw'), ToolMessage(content="Major requirements for 'electrical engineering':\n{'total_points': 128, 'degree_type': 'BS', 'core_courses': {'intro': ['ELEN E1201'], 'circuits': ['ELEN E3201', 'ELEN E3331'], 'signals_systems': ['ELEN E3801'], 'electromagnetics': ['ELEN E3401'], 'communications_or_networking': ['ELEN E3701', 'CSEE W4119'], 'computer_systems': ['CSEE W3827'], 'professional_practice': ['ELEN E3399'], 'senior_design': ['ELEN E3390']}, 'labs': {'required': ['ELEN E3081', 'ELEN E3084', 'ELEN E3083', 'ELEN E3082', 'ELEN E3043'], 'notes': 'Take labs with corresponding lecture courses when possible'}, 'math_science': {'calculus': ['MATH UN1101', 'MATH UN1102'], 'multivariable': ['APMA E2000', 'APMA E2001'], 'differential_equations': {'default': ['APMA E2101'], 'alternative': ['MATH UN2030', 'APMA E3101 or MATH UN2010']}, 'probability': {'choose_one': ['IEOR E3658', 'STAT GU4203'], 'notes': 'STAT GU4001 / SIEO W3600 generally not accepted as substitutes'}, 'physics': {'choose_one_sequence': {'sequence_1': ['PHYS UN1401', 'PHYS UN1402', 'PHYS UN1403'], 'sequence_2': ['PHYS UN1601', 'PHYS UN1602', 'PHYS UN2601'], 'sequence_3': ['PHYS UN2801', 'PHYS UN2802', 'PHYS UN3081']}, 'lab': {'default': ['PHYS UN1494'], 'substitution_note': 'CHEM UN1500 may substitute for physics lab (not generally recommended)', 'substitute': ['CHEM UN1500']}}, 'chemistry': {'lecture_choose_one': ['CHEM UN1403', 'CHEM UN1404', 'CHEM UN2045', 'CHEM UN1604']}, 'computer_science': {'data_structures_choose_one': ['COMS W3134', 'COMS W3136', 'COMS W3137'], 'notes': 'If planning a CS minor, prefer COMS W3134 or COMS W3137'}}, 'technical_electives': {'total_points': 18, 'constraints': {'ee_courses_must_be_3000_level_or_above': True, 'no_significant_overlap': True, 'advisor_approval_if_not_clearly_listed': True}, 'depth': {'points': 6, 'requirement': '>=6 points of EE courses in ONE chosen depth area', 'areas': ['photonics, solid-state devices, and electromagnetics', 'circuits and electronics', 'signals and systems', 'communications and networking']}, 'breadth': {'points': 6, 'requirement': '>=6 points OUTSIDE chosen depth area with significant engineering content'}, 'other': {'points': 6, 'requirement': 'Any additional technical courses to reach 18 total (engineering not required unless missing ELEN E1201)'}}, 'nontechnical': {'total_points': 27, 'required': {'university_writing': ['ENGL CC1010'], 'core_humanities_sequence_choose_one': {'literature_humanities': ['HUMA CC1001', 'HUMA CC1002'], 'contemporary_civilization': ['COCI CC1101', 'COCI CC1102'], 'global_core': 'Two approved Global Core courses (letter grade)'}, 'art_or_music_choose_one': ['HUMA UN1121', 'HUMA UN1123'], 'economics': ['ECON UN1105']}, 'electives': {'points': '9–11', 'rule': 'Choose from SEAS-approved nontechnical elective list (List B); cannot be modified by advisors'}, 'notes': 'Required nontechnical courses are 16–18 points (List A) + 9–11 elective points (List B) = at least 27 total'}, 'other_requirements': {'art_of_engineering': ['ENGI E1102'], 'physical_education': ['PHED UN1001', 'PHED UN1002']}, 'notes': {'early_start': 'ELEN E1201 can be taken as early as first year (typically spring)', 'transfer_students': {'plan_1': 'No ELEN E1201 equivalent — cannot choose circuits & electronics as depth area', 'plan_2': 'Has ELEN E1201 equivalent — can choose circuits & electronics as depth area'}, 'technical_elective_waiver': {'condition': 'If APMA E2101 replaced by MATH UN2030 + Linear Algebra', 'effect': 'Technical electives reduced from 18 to 15 points'}}}\nSource: [220, 221, 222, 223, 224, 225, 226]\n", name='lookup_major', id='a6279e26-946e-470f-a352-d45900af4b80', tool_call_id='toolu_01EPsprkHTCfLKvnEC6QeTud'), ToolMessage(content='{"total_points_required": 27, "lists": {"A_required_nontechnical": {"points_required": {"min": 16, "max": 18}, "rules": ["Must be taken at Columbia.", "All components are required for Engineering students.", "Neither List A nor List B may be modified by advisers."], "components": {"university_writing": ["ENGL CC1010"], "literature_or_civilization_sequence": {"choose_one": [{"id": "literature_humanities", "courses": ["HUMA CC1001", "HUMA CC1002"], "points": 6}, {"id": "contemporary_civilization", "courses": ["COCI CC1101", "COCI CC1102"], "points": 6}, {"id": "global_core_substitution", "rule": "Two approved Global Core courses taken for a letter grade.", "points": {"min": 6, "max": 8}}]}, "art_or_music_humanities": {"choose_one": ["HUMA UN1121", "HUMA UN1123"]}, "principles_of_economics": {"course": "ECON UN1105", "notes": ["May be satisfied through AP credit.", "Barnard substitutes are not permitted."]}}}, "B_elective_nontechnical": {"points_required": {"min": 9, "max": 11}, "rules": ["Must be chosen from the approved List B departmental rules.", "Professional/workshop/lab/project/scientific/studio/music-instruction/master’s-level professional courses do not count.", "AP credit in appropriate subject areas may apply toward the elective nontechnical requirement."], "departmental_rules_reference": "course_eligibility_rules"}}}', name='lookup_school_wide_requirements', id='1cc5dd0c-94d7-417f-9cab-ee34599df59c', tool_call_id='toolu_01LNYHkspFNRKAeMAtWYpm1e'), ToolMessage(content='{"required_course": ["ENGI E1102"], "technical_areas": ["engineering", "mathematics", "physics", "chemistry", "computer_science"], "notes": ["ENGI E1102 (The Art of Engineering) is required of all first-year Engineering students.", "Departments may recommend or require certain technical courses earlier for efficiency."]}', name='lookup_school_wide_requirements', id='4adb4b5c-ac6c-4e51-93b6-9aa130ffeb21', tool_call_id='toolu_013k4uoY3JddS6cU97qZwqR3'), AIMessage(content=[{'text': 'Now let me search for courses that are particularly relevant for an FPGA engineer at an HFT (High-Frequency Trading) firm:', 'type': 'text', 'index': 0}, {'id': 'toolu_01HtkJSS6qwH1H4JnY3GHkeB', 'input': {}, 'name': 'search_courses', 'type': 'tool_use', 'index': 1, 'partial_json': '{"input": {"query":"FPGA digital design hardware","limit":10}}'}, {'id': 'toolu_01NvK2V6C5BicRkPURSVqVKj', 'input': {}, 'name': 'search_courses', 'type': 'tool_use', 'index': 2, 'partial_json': '{"input": {"query":"VHDL Verilog hardware description language","limit":10}}'}, {'id': 'toolu_017F3sbvzDamdNj65f6D8WUC', 'input': {}, 'name': 'search_courses', 'type': 'tool_use', 'index': 3, 'partial_json': '{"input": {"query":"computer architecture hardware systems","limit":10}}'}, {'id': 'toolu_01CyLVgygtsCe1T8D8b3LZpZ', 'input': {}, 'name': 'search_courses', 'type': 'tool_use', 'index': 4, 'partial_json': '{"input": {"query":"high performance computing parallel processing","limit":10}}'}, {'id': 'toolu_01HE6nFTu5eSdwpYhGCMc6fr', 'input': {}, 'name': 'search_courses', 'type': 'tool_use', 'index': 5, 'partial_json': '{"input": {"query":"algorithms data structures optimization","limit":10}}'}], additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={'model_name': 'claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929', 'model_provider': 'anthropic', 'stop_reason': 'tool_use', 'stop_sequence': None}, id='lc_run--019b9093-d229-7831-baff-6dc0aac3046e', tool_calls=[{'name': 'search_courses', 'args': {'input': {'query': 'FPGA digital design hardware', 'limit': 10}}, 'id': 'toolu_01HtkJSS6qwH1H4JnY3GHkeB', 'type': 'tool_call'}, {'name': 'search_courses', 'args': {'input': {'query': 'VHDL Verilog hardware description language', 'limit': 10}}, 'id': 'toolu_01NvK2V6C5BicRkPURSVqVKj', 'type': 'tool_call'}, {'name': 'search_courses', 'args': {'input': {'query': 'computer architecture hardware systems', 'limit': 10}}, 'id': 'toolu_017F3sbvzDamdNj65f6D8WUC', 'type': 'tool_call'}, {'name': 'search_courses', 'args': {'input': {'query': 'high performance computing parallel processing', 'limit': 10}}, 'id': 'toolu_01CyLVgygtsCe1T8D8b3LZpZ', 'type': 'tool_call'}, {'name': 'search_courses', 'args': {'input': {'query': 'algorithms data structures optimization', 'limit': 10}}, 'id': 'toolu_01HE6nFTu5eSdwpYhGCMc6fr', 'type': 'tool_call'}], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 4691, 'output_tokens': 303, 'total_tokens': 4994, 'input_token_details': {'cache_creation': 0, 'cache_read': 0}}), ToolMessage(content='{"courses": [{"course_title": "Analog-Digital Interfaces in VLSI", "course_code": "ELEN E6316", "department": "Electrical Engineering", "department_code": "ELEN", "points": "3", "instructor": "Timothy Dickson", "scheduled_time_start": 420, "scheduled_time_end": 570, "scheduled_days": "T", "type": "LECTURE", "content": "Analog-Digital Interfaces in VLSI (ELEN E6316)\\n        Course Subtitle: Analog-Digital Interfaces\\n        Description: Analog-to-digital and digital-to-analog conversion techniques for very large scale integrated circuits and systems. Precision sampling; quantization; A/D and D/A converter architectures and metrics; Nyquist architectures; oversampling architectures; correction techniques; system considerations. A design project is an integral part of this course.\\n        Prerequisites: \\n    ", "similarity_score": 1.1390514373779297}, {"course_title": "VLSI DESIGN LABORATORY", "course_code": "ELEN E6350", "department": "Electrical Engineering", "department_code": "ELEN", "points": "3", "instructor": "Mingoo Seok", "scheduled_time_start": 880, "scheduled_time_end": 955, "scheduled_days": "TR", "type": "LABORATORY", "content": "VLSI DESIGN LABORATORY (ELEN E6350)\\n        Course Subtitle: \\n        Description: Design of a CMOS mixed-signal integrated circuit. The class divides up into teams to work on mixed-signal integrated circuit designs. The chips are fabricated to be tested the following term. Lectures cover use of computer-aided design tools, design issues specific to the projects, and chip integration issues. This course shares lectures with E4350, but the complexity requirements of integrated circuits are higher...", "similarity_score": 1.2171201705932617}, {"course_title": "PHOTONIC INTEGRATED CIRCUITS", "course_code": "ELEN E6414", "department": "Electrical Engineering", "department_code": "ELEN", "points": "3", "instructor": "Michal Lipson", "scheduled_time_start": 970, "scheduled_time_end": 1120, "scheduled_days": "W", "type": "LECTURE", "content": "PHOTONIC INTEGRATED CIRCUITS (ELEN E6414)\\n        Course Subtitle: PHOTONIC INTEGRATED CIRCU\\n        Description: Photonic integrated circuits are important subsystem components for telecommunications, optically controlled radar, optical signal processing, and photonic local area networks. An introduction to the devices and the design of these circuits. Principle and modeling of dielectric waveguides (including silica on silicon and InP based materials), waveguide devices (simple and star couple...", "similarity_score": 1.2714366912841797}, {"course_title": "DIGITAL SYSTEMS LABORATORY", "course_code": "ELEN E3082", "department": "Electrical Engineering", "department_code": "ELEN", "points": "1", "instructor": "Kenneth Shepard", "scheduled_time_start": 250, "scheduled_time_end": 400, "scheduled_days": "M", "type": "LABORATORY", "content": "DIGITAL SYSTEMS LABORATORY (ELEN E3082)\\n        Course Subtitle: DIGITAL SYSTEMS LABORATOR\\n        Description: Companion lab course for CSEE W3827. Experiments cover such topics as logic gates; flip-flops; shift registers; counters; combinational logic circuits; sequential logic circuits; programmable logic devices. The lab generally meets on alternate weeks.\\n        Prerequisites: CSEE W3827\\n    ", "similarity_score": 1.3084306716918945}, {"course_title": "COMMUNICATION CIRCUITS", "course_code": "ELEN E4314", "department": "Electrical Engineering", "department_code": "ELEN", "points": "3", "instructor": "Emily Naviasky", "scheduled_time_start": 250, "scheduled_time_end": 400, "scheduled_days": "R", "type": "LECTURE", "content": "COMMUNICATION CIRCUITS (ELEN E4314)\\n        Course Subtitle: \\n        Description: Principles of electronic circuits used in the generation, transmission, and reception of signal waveforms, as used in analog and digital communication systems. Nonlinearity and distortion; power amplifiers; tuned amplifiers; oscillators; multipliers and mixers; modulators and demodulators; phase-locked loops. An extensive design project is an integral part of the course.\\n        Prerequisites: \\n    ", "similarity_score": 1.3107632398605347}, {"course_title": "ADV ANALOG INTEGRATED CIRCUITS", "course_code": "ELEN E6312", "department": "Electrical Engineering", "department_code": "ELEN", "points": "3", "instructor": "Harish Krishnaswamy", "scheduled_time_start": 250, "scheduled_time_end": 400, "scheduled_days": "T", "type": "LECTURE", "content": "ADV ANALOG INTEGRATED CIRCUITS (ELEN E6312)\\n        Course Subtitle: ADV ANALOG INTEGRATED CIR\\n        Description: Integrated circuit device characteristics and models; temperature- and supply-independent biasing; IC operational amplifier analysis and design and their applications; feedback amplifiers, stability and frequency compensation techniques; noise in circuits and low-noise design; mismatch in circuits and low-offset design. Computer-aided analysis techniques are used in homework(s) or ...", "similarity_score": 1.3218504190444946}, {"course_title": "DIGITAL COMMUNICATIONS", "course_code": "ELEN E4702", "department": "Electrical Engineering", "department_code": "ELEN", "points": "3", "instructor": "Alexei Ashikhmin", "scheduled_time_start": 420, "scheduled_time_end": 570, "scheduled_days": "W", "type": "LECTURE", "content": "DIGITAL COMMUNICATIONS (ELEN E4702)\\n        Course Subtitle: \\n        Description: Digital communications for both point-to-point and switched applications is further developed. Optimum receiver structures and transmitter signal shaping for both binary and M-ary signal transmission. An introduction to block codes and convolutional codes, with application to space communications.\\n        Prerequisites: \\n    ", "similarity_score": 1.3696717023849487}, {"course_title": "DIGITAL IMAGE PROCESSING", "course_code": "ELEN E4830", "department": "Electrical Engineering", "department_code": "ELEN", "points": "3", "instructor": "Christine P Hendon", "scheduled_time_start": 610, "scheduled_time_end": 760, "scheduled_days": "W", "type": "LECTURE", "content": "DIGITAL IMAGE PROCESSING (ELEN E4830)\\n        Course Subtitle: \\n        Description: Introduction to the mathematical tools and algorithmic implementation for representation and processing of digital pictures, videos, and visual sensory data. Image representation, filtering, transform, quality enhancement, restoration, feature extraction, object segmentation, motion analysis, classification, and coding for data compression. A series of programming assignments reinforces material from the lecture...", "similarity_score": 1.3762567043304443}, {"course_title": "TOPICS IN SIGNAL PROCESSING", "course_code": "ELEN E6883", "department": "Electrical Engineering", "department_code": "ELEN", "points": "3", "instructor": "", "scheduled_time_start": 490, "scheduled_time_end": 600, "scheduled_days": "F", "type": "LECTURE", "content": "TOPICS IN SIGNAL PROCESSING (ELEN E6883)\\n        Course Subtitle: INTRO TO BLOCKCHAIN TECH\\n        Description: Advanced topics in signal processing, such as multidimensional signal processing, image feature extraction, image/video editing and indexing, advanced digital filter design, multirate signal processing, adaptive signal processing, and wave-form coding of signals. Content varies from year to year, and different topics rotate through the course numbers 6880 to 6889.\\n        Prerequisites...", "similarity_score": 1.3977580070495605}, {"course_title": "ELECTRONIC CIRCUITS", "course_code": "ELEN E3331", "department": "Electrical Engineering", "department_code": "ELEN", "points": "3", "instructor": "David G Vallancourt", "scheduled_time_start": 700, "scheduled_time_end": 775, "scheduled_days": "MW", "type": "LECTURE", "content": "ELECTRONIC CIRCUITS (ELEN E3331)\\n        