ion sets, ALU’s, single-cycle and multi-cycle processor design, introduction to pipelined processors, caches, and virtual memory.", "instructor": "Daniel S Rubenstein", "scheduled_time_start": "10:10am", "scheduled_time_end": "11:25am", "call_number": 12394, "campus": NaN, "class_id": "W3827-20261-001", "course_subtitle": "FUNDAMENTALS OF COMPUTER", "department": "Computer Science", "department_code": "CSEE", "link": "https://doc.sis.columbia.edu/subj/CSEE/W3827-20261-001/", "location": "To be announced", "method_of_instruction": "In-Person", "open_to": NaN, "points": "3", "prerequisites": NaN, "scheduled_days": "TR", "section_key": "20261CSEE3827W001", "type": "LECTURE"}, {"course_code": "CSEE W3827", "course_title": "FUNDAMENTALS OF COMPUTER SYSTS", "course_descr": "Fundamentals of computer organization and digital logic. Boolean algebra, Karnaugh maps, basic gates and components, flipflops and latches, counters and state machines, basics of combinational and sequential digital design. Assembly language, instruction sets, ALU’s, single-cycle and multi-cycle processor design, introduction to pipelined processors, caches, and virtual memory.", "instructor": "Daniel S Rubenstein", "scheduled_time_start": "11:40am", "scheduled_time_end": "12:55pm", "call_number": 12395, "campus": NaN, "class_id": "W3827-20261-002", "course_subtitle": "FUNDAMENTALS OF COMPUTER", "department": "Computer Science", "department_code": "CSEE", "link": "https://doc.sis.columbia.edu/subj/CSEE/W3827-20261-002/", "location": "To be announced", "method_of_instruction": "In-Person", "open_to": NaN, "points": "3", "prerequisites": NaN, "scheduled_days": "TR", "section_key": "20261CSEE3827W002", "type": "LECTURE"}]}', name='lookup_course', id='94d6e79e-1bf6-4c3d-b1ee-cabbe614d729', tool_call_id='toolu_01HCgasJu37rfyP1qr9HENpX'), ToolMessage(content='{"courses": [{"course_title": "PRIVACY IN A NETWORKED WORLD", "course_code": "COMS BC3420", "department": "Computer Science @Barnard", "department_code": "COMS", "points": "4", "instructor": "Lucy Simko", "scheduled_time_start": 540, "scheduled_time_end": 650, "scheduled_days": "T", "type": "SEMINAR", "content": "PRIVACY IN A NETWORKED WORLD (COMS BC3420)\\n        Course Subtitle: PRIVACY IN A NETWORKED WO\\n        Description: The ubiquity of computers and networks in business, government, recreation, and almost all aspects of daily life has led to a proliferation of online sensitive data: data that, if used improperly, can harm the data subjects. As a result, concern about the use, ownership, control, privacy, and accuracy of these data has become a top priority. This seminar course focuses on both the t...", "similarity_score": 1.3422341346740723}, {"course_title": "Networks, Crowds, and the Web", "course_code": "COMS W4223", "department": "Computer Science", "department_code": "COMS", "points": "3", "instructor": "Augustin Chaintreau", "scheduled_time_start": 250, "scheduled_time_end": 325, "scheduled_days": "TR", "type": "LECTURE", "content": "Networks, Crowds, and the Web (COMS W4223)\\n        Course Subtitle: NETWORKS CROWDS AND THE W\\n        Description: Introduces fundamental ideas and algorithms on networks of information collected by online services. It covers properties pervasive in large networks, dynamics of individuals that lead to large collective phenomena, mechanisms underlying the web economy, and results and tools informing societal impact of algorithms on privacy, polarization and discrimination.\\n        Prerequisites: ...", "similarity_score": 1.3480324745178223}, {"course_title": "HARDWARE SECURITY", "course_code": "COMS E6424", "department": "Computer Science", "department_code": "COMS", "points": "3", "instructor": "Simha Sethumadhavan", "scheduled_time_start": 610, "scheduled_time_end": 685, "scheduled_days": "MW", "type": "LECTURE", "content": "HARDWARE SECURITY (COMS E6424)\\n        Course Subtitle: \\n        Description: \\n        Prerequisites: \\n    ", "similarity_score": 