: 4691, 'output_tokens': 303, 'total_tokens': 4994, 'input_token_details': {'cache_creation': 0, 'cache_read': 0}}), ToolMessage(content='{"courses": [{"course_title": "Analog-Digital Interfaces in VLSI", "course_code": "ELEN E6316", "department": "Electrical Engineering", "department_code": "ELEN", "points": "3", "instructor": "Timothy Dickson", "scheduled_time_start": 420, "scheduled_time_end": 570, "scheduled_days": "T", "type": "LECTURE", "content": "Analog-Digital Interfaces in VLSI (ELEN E6316)\\n        Course Subtitle: Analog-Digital Interfaces\\n        Description: Analog-to-digital and digital-to-analog conversion techniques for very large scale integrated circuits and systems. Precision sampling; quantization; A/D and D/A converter architectures and metrics; Nyquist architectures; oversampling architectures; correction techniques; system considerations. A design project is an integral part of this course.\\n        Prerequisites: \\n    ", "similarity_score": 1.1390514373779297}, {"course_title": "VLSI DESIGN LABORATORY", "course_code": "ELEN E6350", "department": "Electrical Engineering", "department_code": "ELEN", "points": "3", "instructor": "Mingoo Seok", "scheduled_time_start": 880, "scheduled_time_end": 955, "scheduled_days": "TR", "type": "LABORATORY", "content": "VLSI DESIGN LABORATORY (ELEN E6350)\\n        Course Subtitle: \\n        Description: Design of a CMOS mixed-signal integrated circuit. The class divides up into teams to work on mixed-signal integrated circuit designs. The chips are fabricated to be tested the following term. Lectures cover use of computer-aided design tools, design issues specific to the projects, and chip integration issues. This course shares lectures with E4350, but the complexity requirements of integrated circuits are higher...", "similarity_score": 1.2171201705932617}, {"course_title": "PHOTONIC INTEGRATED CIRCUITS", "course_code": "ELEN E6414", "department": "Electrical Engineering", "department_code": "ELEN", 