 + 9–11 elective points (List B) = at least 27 total'}, 'other_requirements': {'art_of_engineering': ['ENGI E1102'], 'physical_education': ['PHED UN1001', 'PHED UN1002']}, 'notes': {'early_start': 'ELEN E1201 can be taken as early as first year (typically spring)', 'transfer_students': {'plan_1': 'No ELEN E1201 equivalent — cannot choose circuits & electronics as depth area', 'plan_2': 'Has ELEN E1201 equivalent — can choose circuits & electronics as depth area'}, 'technical_elective_waiver': {'condition': 'If APMA E2101 replaced by MATH UN2030 + Linear Algebra', 'effect': 'Technical electives reduced from 18 to 15 points'}}}\nSource: [220, 221, 222, 223, 224, 225, 226]\n", name='lookup_major', id='59a05f21-1888-4aa0-9dbf-61841cfefa11', tool_call_id='toolu_01BACTAyEpkKC46JKnyk2Xd1'), ToolMessage(content='{"total_points_required": 27, "lists": {"A_required_nontechnical": {"points_required": {"min": 16, "max": 18}, "rules": ["Must be taken at Columbia.", "All components are required for Engineering students.", "Neither List A nor List B may be modified by advisers."], "components": {"university_writing": ["ENGL CC1010"], "literature_or_civilization_sequence": {"choose_one": [{"id": "literature_humanities", "courses": ["HUMA CC1001", "HUMA CC1002"], "points": 6}, {"id": "contemporary_civilization", "courses": ["COCI CC1101", "COCI CC1102"], "points": 6}, {"id": "global_core_substitution", "rule": "Two approved Global Core courses taken for a letter grade.", "points": {"min": 6, "max": 8}}]}, "art_or_music_humanities": {"choose_one": ["HUMA UN1121", "HUMA UN1123"]}, "principles_of_economics": {"course": "ECON UN1105", "notes": ["May be satisfied through AP credit.", "Barnard substitutes are not permitted."]}}}, "B_elective_nontechnical": {"points_required": {"min": 9, "max": 11}, "rules": ["Must be chosen from the approved List B departmental rules.", "Professional/workshop/lab/project/scientific/studio/music-instruction/master’s-level professional courses do not count.", "AP credit in appropriate subject areas may apply toward the elective nontechnical requirement."], "departmental_rules_reference": "course_eligibility_rules"}}}', name='lookup_school_wide_requirements', id='730fc570-35d4-4f65-ac1b-52d2a95c48d7', tool_call_id='toolu_01RvtU2N3HFKHeFhfWtkgAFC'), ToolMessage(content='{"required_course": ["ENGI E1102"], "technical_areas": ["engineering", "mathematics", "physics", "chemistry", "computer_science"], "notes": ["ENGI E1102 (The Art of Engineering) is required of all first-year Engineering students.", "Departments may recommend or require certain technical courses earlier for efficiency."]}', name='lookup_school_wide_requirements', id='307fe129-74b0-4484-8b71-2e9fcd1c6bea', tool_call_id='toolu_01DBXcoSGqsgteAFowr4E9Du'), HumanMessage(content='tell me ee requirements', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='3d1c8d2e-21b8-49a6-89a8-e2959c4254be')], 'user_id': 'nl2951@columbia.edu', 'name': None, 'school': None, 'department_of_major': None, 'major': None, 'completed_courses': [], 'semester': None, 'career_goals': [], 'preferences': [], 'thread_tool_call_count': {'get_user_profile': 1, 'lookup_school_wide_requirements': 4, 'lookup_major': 2, '__all__': 16}}}, 'run_id': '019b909e-7bab-7ef0-9e93-f84a129da9fc', 'name': 'model', 'tags': ['graph:step:36'], 'metadata': {'thread_id': '2de77b04-7c32-47ec-84dc-81f3861507d4', 'langgraph_step': 36, 'langgraph_node': 'model', 'langgraph_triggers': ('branch:to:model',), 'langgraph_path': ('__pregel_pull', 'model'), 'langgraph_checkpoint_ns': 'model:14f9c76f-cd22-03e2-aca6-04dd3fc9eb8a', 'LANGSMITH_TRACING': 'true', 'revision_id': 'db347d5-dirty'}, 'parent_ids': ['019b909e-7ba9-7382-a9a2-4ee8a3cad85c']}
{'event': 'on_chain_stream', 'run_id': '019b909e-7ba9-7382-a9a2-4ee8a3cad85c', 'name': 'LangGraph', 'tags': [], 'metadata': {'thread_id': '2de77b04-7c32-47ec-84dc-81f3861507d4'}, 'data': {'chunk': {'model': {'messages': [AIMessage(content=[{'text': 'Based on the bulletin information I retrieved, here are the **complete Electrical Engineering (EE) major requirements** for the BS degree:\n\n---\n\n## **Total Points Required: 128**\n\n---\n\n## **1. EE CORE COURSES**\n\n### **Required Core Courses:**\n- **ELEN E1201** - Introduction to Electrical Engineering\n- **ELEN E3201** - Circuit Analysis\n- **ELEN E3331** - Electronic Circuits\n- **ELEN E3801** - Signals and Systems\n- **ELEN E3401** - Electromagnetics\n- **CSEE W3827** - Fundamentals of Computer Systems\n- **ELEN E3399** - Professional Practice (0 credits)\n- **ELEN E3390** - Senior Design (capstone project)\n\n### **Communications/Networking (choose one):**\n- **ELEN E3701** - Communications\n- **CSEE W4119** - Computer Networks\n\n---\n\n## **2. REQUIRED LABS (5 labs total)**\nMust be taken with corresponding lecture courses when possible:\n- **ELEN E3081** - Circuits Lab\n- **ELEN E3084** - Electronics Lab\n- **ELEN E3082** - Digital Systems Lab\n- **ELEN E3083** - Signals & Systems Lab\n- **ELEN E3043** - Electromagnetics Lab\n\n---\n\n## **3. MATH & SCIENCE REQUIREMENTS**\n\n### **Mathematics:**\n- **MATH UN1101** - Calculus I\n- **MATH UN1102** - Calculus II\n- **APMA E2000** - Multivariable Calculus for Engineers & Applied Scientists\n- **APMA E2001** - Multivariable Calculus Continued\n\n### **Differential Equations (choose one):**\n- **APMA E2101** - ODEs & Linear Algebra (recommended)\n- OR **MATH UN2030** + Linear Algebra course\n\n### **Probability (choose one):**\n- **IEOR E3658** - Probability & Statistics for Engineers\n- **STAT GU4203** - Probability Theory\n- ⚠️ Note: STAT GU4001 / SIEO W3600 generally NOT accepted\n\n### **Physics (choose one sequence):**\n**Sequence 1 (most common):**\n- **PHYS UN1401** - Mechanics\n- **PHYS UN1402** - Electricity & Magnetism\n- **PHYS UN1403** - Waves, Optics & Thermodynamics\n\n**Sequence 2:**\n- PHYS UN1601, UN1602, UN2601\n\n**Sequence 3:**\n- PHYS UN2801, UN2802, UN3081\n\n### **Physics Lab:**\n- **PHYS UN1494** - Physics Lab\n- OR **CHEM UN1500** (chemistry lab - not recommended)\n\n### **Chemistry (choose one):**\n- **CHEM UN1403** - General Chemistry I\n- **CHEM UN1404** - General Chemistry II\n- **CHEM UN2045** - Intensive General Chemistry\n- **CHEM UN1604** - Chemistry: Green Energy & Sustainability\n\n### **Computer Science - Data Structures (choose one):**\n- **COMS W3134** - Data Structures in Java\n- **COMS W3136** - Data Structures (honors)\n- **COMS W3137** - Data Structures & Algorithms\n\n---\n\n## **4. TECHNICAL ELECTIVES (18 points total)**\n\nMust choose 18 points following these constraints:\n\n### **Depth Requirement (6 points):**\nAt least 6 points of EE courses (3000-level or above) in ONE depth area:\n1. **Photonics, Solid-State Devices, and Electromagnetics**\n2. **Circuits and Electronics**\n3. **Signals and Systems**\n4. **Communications and Networking**\n\n### **Breadth Requirement (6 points):**\nAt least 6 points OUTSIDE your chosen depth area with significant engineering content\n\n### **Other Technical Electives (6 points):**\nAny additional technical courses to reach 18 total points\n- Engineering content not required UNLESS you\'re missing ELEN E1201\n\n### **Constraints:**\n- EE courses must be 3000-level or above\n- No significant overlap between courses\n- Advisor approval required if courses not clearly on approved list\n\n---\n\n## **5. NONTECHNICAL REQUIREMENTS (27 points total)**\n\n### **Required Nontechnical (List A: 16-18 points):**\n\n**University Writing:**\n- **ENGL CC1010** - University Writing\n\n**Core Humanities Sequence (choose ONE option):**\n- **HUMA CC1001 & CC1002** - Literature Humanities I & II (6 pts)\n- **COCI CC1101 & CC1102** - Contemporary Civilization I & II (6 pts)\n- **Two approved Global Core courses** (letter grade, 6-8 pts)\n\n**Art or Music Humanities (choose one):**\n- **HUMA UN1121** - Masterpieces of Western Art\n- **HUMA UN1123** - Masterpieces of Western Music\n\n**Economics:**\n- **ECON UN1105** - Principles of Economics\n  - May be satisfied through AP credit\n  - Barnard substitutes NOT permitted\n\n### **Elective Nontechnical (List B: 9-11 points):**\n- Must be chosen from SEAS-approved List B\n- Cannot be professional/workshop/lab/project courses\n- AP credit may apply\n\n---\n\n## **6. OTHER REQUIREMENTS**\n\n### **First-Year Engineering:**\n- **ENGI E1102** - The Art of Engineering (required for all first-year SEAS students)\n\n### **Physical Education:**\n- **PHED UN1001** - PE\n- **PHED UN1002** - PE\n\n---\n\n## **IMPORTANT NOTES:**\n\n1. **Early Start:** ELEN E1201 can be taken as early as first year (typically spring semester)\n\n2. **Technical Elective Waiver:** If you take MATH UN2030 + Linear Algebra instead of APMA E2101, your technical electives reduce from 18 to 15 points\n\n3. **Transfer Students:**\n   - Without ELEN E1201 equivalent → cannot choose "Circuits & Electronics" as depth area\n   - With ELEN E1201 equivalent → can choose any depth area\n\n4. **CS Minor:** If planning a CS minor, prefer COMS W3134 or COMS W3137 for data structures\n\n---\n\nDoes this help clarify the requirements? Would you like me to create a specific 8-semester plan for your FPGA/HFT career goal?', 'type': 'text', 'index': 0}], additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={'model_name': 'claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929', 'model_provider': 'anthropic', 'stop_reason': 'end_turn', 'stop_sequence': None}, id='lc_run--019b909e-7bb8-7890-94d6-aa9feba70740', usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 23975, 'output_tokens': 1617, 'total_tokens': 25592, 'input_token_details': {'cache_creation': 0, 'cache_read': 0}})]}}}, 'parent_ids': []}
