d data structures\n- Some finance background\n\nHere's your recommended **8-semester plan as an Electrical Engineering major**:\n\n## **Semester 1 (Fall, First Year)**\n| Course Code | Course Title | Points | Notes |\n|------------|--------------|---------|--------|\n| ENGI E1102 | Art of Engineering | 3 | Required for all SEAS students |\n| MATH UN1101 | Calculus I | 3 | Math/Science requirement |\n| PHYS UN1401 | Physics I (Mechanics) | 3 | Physics sequence |\n| CHEM UN1403 | General Chemistry I | 3 | Chemistry requirement |\n| ENGL CC1010 | University Writing | 3 | Nontechnical requirement |\n| PHED UN1001 | Physical Education | 0 | PE requirement |\n| **Total** | | **15** | |\n\n## **Semester 2 (Spring, First Year)**\n| Course Code | Course Title | Points | Notes |\n|------------|--------------|---------|--------|\n| ELEN E1201 | Introduction to Electrical Engineering | 3 | EE core intro course |\n| MATH UN1102 | Calculus II | 3 | Math/Science requirement |\n| PHYS UN1402 | Physics II (E&M) | 3 | Physics sequence |\n| PHYS UN1494 | Physics Lab | 1 | Physics lab requirement |\n| HUMA CC1001 | Literature Humanities I | 3 | Nontechnical requirement |\n| PHED UN1002 | Physical Education | 0 | PE requirement |\n| **Total** | | **13** | |\n\n## **Semester 3 (Fall, Second Year)**\n| Course Code | Course Title | Points | Notes |\n|------------|--------------|---------|--------|\n| ELEN E3201 | Circuit Analysis | 3 | EE core circuits |\n| ELEN E3081 | Circuits Lab | 1 | Required lab |\n| APMA E2000 | Multivariable Calculus | 3 | Math/Science requirement |\n| PHYS UN1403 | Physics III (Waves/Optics) | 3 | Physics sequence |\n| COMS W3134 | Data Structures in Java | 3 | CS requirement - crucial for HFT |\n| HUMA CC1002 | Literature Humanities II | 3 | Nontechnical requirement |\n| **Total** | | **16** | |\n\n## **Semester 4 (Spring, Second Year)**\n| Course Code | Course Title | Points | Notes |\n|------------|--------------|---------|--------|\n| ELEN E3331 | Electronic Circuits | 3 | EE core circuits |\n| ELEN E3084 | Electronics Lab | 1 | Required lab |\n| CSEE W3827 | Fundamentals of Computer Systems | 3 | EE core - **CRITICAL for FPGA** |\n| ELEN E3082 | Digital Systems Lab | 1 | Required lab - **CRITICAL for FPGA** |\n| APMA E2001 | Multivariable Calculus II | 3 | Math/Science requirement |\n| ECON UN1105 | Principles of Economics | 3 | Nontechnical requirement |\n| **Total** | | **14** | |\n\n## **Semester 5 (Fall, Third Year)**\n| Course Code | Course Title | Points | Notes |\n|------------|--------------|---------|--------|\n| ELEN E3401 | Electromagnetics | 3 | EE core |\n| ELEN E3043 | Electromagnetics Lab | 1 | Required lab |\n| ELEN E3801 | Signals and Systems | 3 | EE core |\n| ELEN E3083 | Signals & Systems Lab | 1 | Required lab |\n| APMA E2101 | ODEs & Linear Algebra | 4 | Math/Science requirement |\n| COMS W3157 | Advanced Programming (C/Unix) | 4 | **CRITICAL for HFT - low-level programming** |\n| **Total** | | **16** | |\n\n## **Semester 6 (Spring, Third Year)**\n| Course Code | Course Title | Points | Notes |\n|------------|--------------|---------|--------|\n| ELEN E3399 | Professional Practice | 0 | EE core requirement |\n| CSEE W4119 | Computer Networks | 3 | EE core - **Important for HFT networking** |\n| IEOR E3658 | Probability & Statistics | 3 | Math/Science requirement |\n| ELEN E4350 | VLSI Design Laboratory | 3 | **CRITICAL - FPGA design experience** |\n| COMS W4232 | Advanced Algorithms | 3 | **CRITICAL for HFT - optimization** |\n| HUMA UN1121 or UN1123 | Art/Music Humanities | 3 | Nontechnical requirement |\n| **Total** | | **15** | |\n\n## **Semester 7 (Fall, Fourth Year)**\n| Course Code | Course Title | Points | Notes |\n|------------|--------------|---------|--------|\n| ELEN E3390 | Senior Design I | 3 | EE core capstone |\n| COMS W4118 | Operating Systems | 3 | **Important for systems understanding** |\n| ELEN E4314 | Communication Circuits | 3 | Depth elective (Circuits area) - high-speed circuits |\n| COMS E6424 | Hardware Security | 3 | Breadth elective - FPGA security |\n| Nontechnical Elective | List B Elective | 3 | Nontechnical elective |\n| **Total** | | **15** | |\n\n## **Semester 8 (Spring, Fourth Year)**\n| Course Code | Course Title | Points | Notes |\n|------------|--------------|---------|--------|\n| ELEN E3390 | Senior Design II | 0 | EE core capstone continuation |\n| ELEN E6316 | Analog-Digital Interfaces in VLSI | 3 | Technical elective - ADC/DAC for trading systems |\n| ELEN E4702 | Digital Communications | 3 | Technical elective - high-speed data |\n| Nontechnical Elective | List B Elective | 3 | Nontechnical elective |\n| Nontechnical Elective | List B Elective | 3 | Nontechnical elective |\n| **Total** | | **12** | |\n\n---\n\n## **Summary & Key Points:**\n\n**Total Points: ~131** (exceeds 128 minimum)\n\n### **Why This Plan is Perfect for FPGA Engineering at HFT:**\n\n1. **Digital Design Foundation:**\n   - CSEE W3827 (Computer Systems) + ELEN E3082 (Digital Systems Lab) - You'll learn digital logic, state machines, and hardware design\n   - ELEN E4350 (VLSI Design Lab) - Hands-on FPGA/ASIC design with CAD tools\n\n2. **Low-Level Programming (Critical for HFT):**\n   - COMS W3157 (Advanced Programming) - C programming, Unix, TCP/IP networking\n   - COMS W3134 (Data Structures) - Efficient algorithms\n   - COMS W4232 (Advanced Algorithms) - Optimization techniques used in HFT\n\n3. **High-Performance Systems:**\n   - COMS W4118 (Operating Systems) - Understanding of scheduling, memory management\n   - CSEE W4119 (Computer Networks) - Low-latency networking\n\n4. **Hardware-Software Interface:**\n   - ELEN E6316 (Analog-Digital Interfaces) - ADC/DAC crucial for market data feeds\n   - ELEN E4314 (Communication Circuits) - High-speed circuit design\n   - COMS E6424 (Hardware Security) - FPGA security considerations\n\n5. **Signals & Communications:**\n   - ELEN E3801 (Signals and Systems) - Signal processing fundamentals\n   - ELEN E4702 (Digital Communications) - High-speed data transmission\n\n### **Career Preparation:**\n- Strong C/C++ programming skills (COMS W3157)\n- FPGA design experience (ELEN E4350, CSEE W3827)\n- Algorithm optimization (COMS W4232)\n- Low-latency networking (CSEE W4119, COMS W3157)\n- Hardware-software co-design experience\n\n### **Recommendations:**\n1. **Summer internships:** Seek FPGA or HFT internships after sophomore/junior years\n2. **Side projects:** Build FPGA projects (maybe implement trading algorithms on FPGA)\n3. **Learn HDLs:** Practice Verilog/VHDL outside of class\n4. **Finance knowledge:** Consider auditing finance courses or self-studying market microstructure\n5. **Programming:** Master C++ as it's the primary language in HFT\n\nThis plan balances all EE requirements while giving you the computer science, algorithms, and systems knowledge that HFT firms seek in FPGA engineers!", 'type': 'text', 'index': 0}], additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={'model_name': 'claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929', 'model_provider': 'anthropic', 'stop_reason': 'end_turn', 'stop_sequence': None}, id='lc_run--019b9094-311f-7781-8b0b-b9d9ce04d6bf', usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 19502, 'output_tokens': 2330, 'total_tokens': 21832, 'input_token_details': {'cache_creation': 0, 'cache_read': 0}}), HumanMessage(content='tell me what classes to take in 8 semesters as an ee major. i want to be an FPGA engineer at a HFT firm', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='e5010653-8598-40f9-8b3a-53c2e0559c8e'), AIMessage(content=[{'id': 'toolu_017MrhGFHZZyaTYArubkQp3K', 'input': {}, 'name': 'get_user_profile', 'type': 'tool_use', 'index': 0, 'partial_json': ''}, {'id': 'toolu_01BACTAyEpkKC46JKnyk2Xd1', 'input': {}, 'name': 'lookup_major', 'type': 'tool_use', 'index': 1, 'partial_json': '{"major": "electrical engineering"}'}, {'id': 'toolu_01RvtU2N3HFKHeFhfWtkgAFC', 'input': {}, 'name': 'lookup_school_wide_requirements', 'type': 'tool_use', 'index': 2, 'partial_json': '{"input": {"q