{'event': 'on_chat_model_end', 'data': {'output': AIMessage(content=[{'text': "# Electrical Engineering (EE) Requirements\n\nHere's a comprehensive breakdown of the **BS in Electrical Engineering** requirements at Columbia (128 total points):\n\n---\n\n## **Core EE Courses**\n\n| Course | Title |\n|--------|-------|\n| **ELEN E1201** | Introduction to Electrical Engineering |\n| **ELEN E3201** | Circuits |\n| **ELEN E3331** | Electronics |\n| **ELEN E3801** | Signals and Systems |\n| **ELEN E3401** | Electromagnetics |\n| **ELEN E3701** or **CSEE W4119** | Communications or Networking |\n| **CSEE W3827** | Computer Systems |\n| **ELEN E3399** | Professional Practice |\n| **ELEN E3390** | Senior Design |\n\n---\n\n## **Required Labs** (5 labs)\n- **ELEN E3081, E3082, E3083, E3084, E3043**\n- Take labs with corresponding lecture courses when possible\n\n---\n\n## **Math & Science Requirements**\n\n### **Mathematics:**\n- **Calculus:** MATH UN1101, MATH UN1102\n- **Multivariable:** APMA E2000, APMA E2001\n- **Differential Equations:** APMA E2101 (or alternatives: MATH UN2030, APMA E3101/MATH UN2010)\n- **Probability:** IEOR E3658 or STAT GU4203\n\n### **Physics:** (Choose one sequence)\n- Sequence 1: PHYS UN1401, 1402, 1403\n- Sequence 2: PHYS UN1601, 1602, 2601\n- Sequence 3: PHYS UN2801, 2802, 3081\n- **Physics Lab:** PHYS UN1494 (or CHEM UN1500)\n\n### **Chemistry:** (Choose one)\n- CHEM UN1403, UN1404, UN2045, or UN1604\n\n### **Computer Science:**\n- **Data Structures:** COMS W3134, W3136, or W3137\n  - (If planning a CS minor, prefer W3134 or W3137)\n\n---\n\n## **Technical Electives** (18 points total)\n\nMust be 3000-level or above with no significant overlap:\n\n1. **Depth (6 points):** 6+ points in ONE area:\n   - Photonics, solid-state devices, and electromagnetics\n   - Circuits and electronics\n   - Signals and systems\n   - Communications and networking\n\n2. **Breadth (6 points):** 6+ points OUTSIDE your depth area with significant engineering content\n\n3. **Other (6 points):** Any additional technical courses\n\n---\n\n## **Nontechnical Requirements** (27 points)\n\n### **Required (16-18 points):**\n- **University Writing:** ENGL CC1010\n- **Core Humanities:** Choose one sequence:\n  - Literature Humanities (HUMA CC1001, CC1002) OR\n  - Contemporary Civilization (COCI CC1101, CC1102) OR\n  - Two approved Global Core courses\n- **Art or Music:** HUMA UN1121 or UN1123\n- **Economics:** ECON UN1105\n\n### **Electives (9-11 points):**\n- Choose from SEAS-approved nontechnical elective list (List B)\n\n---\n\n## **Other Requirements**\n- **Art of Engineering:** ENGI E1102\n- **Physical Education:** PHED UN1001, UN1002\n\n---\n\n## **Important Notes:**\n- **ELEN E1201** can be taken as early as first year (typically spring semester)\n- If you replace APMA E2101 with MATH UN2030 + Linear Algebra, technical electives reduce from 18 to 15 points\n- Transfer students without ELEN E1201 equivalent cannot choose circuits & electronics as their depth area\n\nWould you like help planning your specific course schedule or have questions about any of these requirements?", 'type': 'text', 'index': 0}], additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={'model_name': 'claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929', 'model_provider': 'anthropic', 'stop_reason': 'end_turn', 'stop_sequence': None}, id='lc_run--019b90a5-468f-7493-8f18-9648d11e202a', usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 3927, 'output_tokens': 970, 'total_tokens': 4897, 'input_token_details': {'cache_creation': 0, 'cache_read': 0}}), 'input': {'messages': [[SystemMessage(content=[{'type': 'text', 'text': 'You are an expert Columbia University course advisor.\nUse the user profile when answering. \nIf you recommend a class, make sure to check that the user satisfies prerequisites. \nIf a user asks to plan ONLY the next semester, include a timetable where each course has a time slot. \nIf a user asks to plan all of their semesters, do not include times of classes. Include only a list of classes per semester in a table. \n\nIf you are searching up a specific course (to see its timing or prerequisites), use the lookup_course tool. \n- Example: to find information about ELEN E1201 -> lookup_course\n- Example: to find optimization classes that are computational -> search_courses\n\nIf a users current semester is 4, they have 5 semesters remaining. Assume each user graduates in 8 semesters unless stated otherwise. \nUnless stated otherwise, ensure that an individual in SEAS takes 15+ credits, ideally 18+.'}, {'type': 'text', 'text': "\n\n## `write_todos`\n\nYou have access to the `write_todos` tool to help you manage and plan complex objectives.\nUse this tool for complex objectives to ensure that you are tracking each necessary step and giving the user visibility into your progress.\nThis tool is very helpful for planning complex objectives, and for breaking down these larger complex objectives into smaller steps.\n\nIt is critical that you mark todos as completed as soon as you are done with a step. Do not batch up multiple steps before marking them as completed.\nFor simple objectives that only require a few steps, it is better to just complete the objective directly and NOT use this tool.\nWriting todos takes time and tokens, use it when it is helpful for managing complex many-step problems! But not for simple few-step requests.\n\n## Important To-Do List Usage Notes to Remember\n- The `write_todos` tool should never be called multiple times in parallel.\n- Don't be afraid to revise the To-Do list as you go. New information may reveal new tasks that need to be done, or old tasks that are irrelevant."}], additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}), HumanMessage(content='tell me ee requirements', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='23afd3f8-7155-4b00-bac6-21019dc7ece7'), AIMessage(content=[{'id': 'toolu_0195nkfcLMwdcp8e8sRufTe3', 'input': {}, 'name': 'lookup_major', 'type': 'tool_use', 'index': 0, 'partial_json': '{"major": "electrical engineering"}'}], additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={'model_name': 'claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929', 'model_provider': 'anthropic', 'stop_reason': 'tool_use', 'stop_sequence': None}, id='lc_run--019b90a5-3912-7c42-9b02-2d1a63673d06', tool_calls=[{'name': 'lookup_major', 'args': {'major': 'electrical engineering'}, 'id': 'toolu_0195nkfcLMwdcp8e8sRufTe3', 'type': 'tool_call'}], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 2547, 'output_tokens': 54, 'total_tokens': 2601, 'input_token_details': {'cache_creation': 0, 'cache_read': 0}}), ToolMessage(content="Major requirements for 'electrical engineering':\n{'total_points': 128, 'degree_type': 'BS', 'core_courses': {'intro': ['ELEN E1201'], 'circuits': ['ELEN E3201', 'ELEN E3331'], 'signals_systems': ['ELEN E3801'], 'electromagnetics': ['ELEN E3401'], 'communications_or_networking': ['ELEN E3701', 'CSEE W4119'], 'computer_systems': ['CSEE W3827'], 'professional_practice': ['ELEN E3399'], 'senior_design': ['ELEN E3390']}, 'labs': {'required': ['ELEN E3081', 'ELEN E3084', 'ELEN E3083', 'ELEN E3082', 'ELEN E3043'], 'notes': 'Take labs with corresponding lecture courses when possible'}, 'math_science': {'calculus': ['MATH UN1101', 'MATH UN1102'], 'multivariable': ['APMA E2000', 'APMA E2001'], 'differential_equations': {'default': ['APMA E2101'], 'alternative': ['MATH UN2030', 'APMA E3101 or MATH UN2010']}, 'probability': {'choose_one': ['IEOR E3658', 'STAT GU4203'], 'notes': 'STAT GU4001 / SIEO W3600 generally not accepted as substitutes'}, 'physics': {'choose_one_sequence': {'sequence_1': ['PHYS UN1401', 'PHYS UN1402', 'PHYS UN1403'], 'sequence_2': ['PHYS UN1601', 'PHYS UN1602', 'PHYS UN2601'], 'sequence_3': ['PHYS UN2801', 'PHYS UN2802', 'PHYS UN3081']}, 'lab': {'default': ['PHYS UN1494'], 'substitution_note': 'CHEM UN1500 may substitute for physics lab (not generally recommended)', 'substitute': ['CHEM UN1500']}}, 'chemistry': {'lecture_choose_one': ['CHEM UN1403', 'CHEM UN1404', 'CHEM UN2045', 'CHEM UN1604']}, 'computer_science': {'data_structures_choose