tart': 'ELEN E1201 can be taken as early as first year (typically spring)', 'transfer_students': {'plan_1': 'No ELEN E1201 equivalent — cannot choose circuits & electronics as depth area', 'plan_2': 'Has ELEN E1201 equivalent — can choose circuits & electronics as depth area'}, 'technical_elective_waiver': {'condition': 'If APMA E2101 replaced by MATH UN2030 + Linear Algebra', 'effect': 'Technical electives reduced from 18 to 15 points'}}}\nSource: [220, 221, 222, 223, 224, 225, 226]\n", name='lookup_major', id='48015f56-3fa7-4cb3-a920-297595641b6f', tool_call_id='toolu_0195nkfcLMwdcp8e8sRufTe3'), AIMessage(content=[{'text': "# Electrical Engineering (EE) Requirements\n\nHere's a comprehensive breakdown of the **BS in Electrical Engineering** requirements at Columbia (128 total points):\n\n---\n\n## **Core EE Courses**\n\n| Course | Title |\n|--------|-------|\n| **ELEN E1201** | Introduction to Electrical Engineering |\n| **ELEN E3201** | Circuits |\n| **ELEN E3331** | Electronics |\n| **ELEN E3801** | Signals and Systems |\n| **ELEN E3401** | Electromagnetics |\n| **ELEN E3701** or **CSEE W4119** | Communications or Networking |\n| **CSEE W3827** | Computer Systems |\n| **ELEN E3399** | Professional Practice |\n| **ELEN E3390** | Senior Design |\n\n---\n\n## **Required Labs** (5 labs)\n- **ELEN E3081, E3082, E3083, E3084, E3043**\n- Take labs with corresponding lecture courses when possible\n\n---\n\n## **Math & Science Requirements**\n\n### **Mathematics:**\n- **Calculus:** MATH UN1101, MATH UN1102\n- **Multivariable:** APMA E2000, APMA E2001\n- **Differential Equations:** APMA E2101 (or alternatives: MATH UN2030, APMA E3101/MATH UN2010)\n- **Probability:** IEOR E3658 or STAT GU4203\n\n### **Physics:** (Choose one sequence)\n- Sequence 1: PHYS UN1401, 1402, 1403\n- Sequence 2: PHYS UN1601, 1602, 2601\n- Sequence 3: PHYS UN2801, 2802, 3081\n- **Physics Lab:** PHYS UN1494 (or CHEM UN1500)\n\n### **Chemistry:** (Choose one)\n- CHEM UN1403, UN1404, UN2045, or UN1604\n\n### **Computer Science:**\n- **Data Structures:** COMS W3134, W3136, or W3137\n  - (If planning a CS minor, prefer W3134 or W3137)\n\n---\n\n## **Technical Electives** (18 points total)\n\nMust be 3000-level or above with no significant overlap:\n\n1. **Depth (6 points):** 6+ points in ONE area:\n   - Photonics, solid-state devices, and electromagnetics\n   - Circuits and electronics\n   - Signals and systems\n   - Communications and networking\n\n2. **Breadth (6 points):** 6+ points OUTSIDE your depth area with significant engineering content\n\n3. **Other (6 points):** Any additional technical courses\n\n---\n\n## **Nontechnical Requirements** (27 points)\n\n### **Required (16-18 points):**\n- **University Writing:** ENGL CC1010\n- **Core Humanities:** Choose one sequence:\n  - Literature Humanities (HUMA CC1001, CC1002) OR\n  - Contemporary Civilization (COCI CC1101, CC1102) OR\n  - Two approved Global Core courses\n- **Art or Music:** HUMA UN1121 or UN1123\n- **Economics:** ECON UN1105\n\n### **Electives (9-11 points):**\n- Choose from SEAS-approved nontechnical elective list (List B)\n\n---\n\n## **Other Requirements**\n- **Art of Engineering:** ENGI E1102\n- **Physical Education:** PHED UN1001, UN1002\n\n---\n\n## **Important Notes:**\n- **ELEN E1201** can be taken as early as first year (typically spring semester)\n- If you replace APMA E2101 with MATH UN2030 + Linear Algebra, technical electives reduce from 18 to 15 points\n- Transfer students without ELEN E1201 equivalent cannot choose circuits & electronics as their depth area\n\nWould you like help planning your specific course schedule or have questions about any of these requirements?", 'type': 'text', 'index': 0}], additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={'model_name': 'claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929', 'model_provider': 'anthropic', 'stop_reason': 'end_turn', 'stop_sequence': None}, id='lc_run--019b90a5-468f-7493-8f18-9648d11e202a', usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 3927, 'output_tokens': 970, 'total_tokens': 4897, 'input_token_details': {'cache_creation': 0, 'cache_read': 0}})], 'user_id': 'nl2951@columbia.edu', 'name': None, 'school': None, 'department_of_major': None, 'major': None, 'completed_courses': [], 'semester': None, 'career_goals': [], 'preferences': []}}, 'run_id': '019b90a5-38dd-7180-b916-94756159a70b', 'name': 'LangGraph', 'tags': [], 'metadata': {'thread_id': '2de77b04-7c32-47ec-84dc-81f3861507d4', 'LANGSMITH_TRACING': 'true', 'revision_id': 'db347d5-dirty'}, 'parent_ids': []}
